{"repo": "agentscope-ai/agentscope", "pull_number": 3978, "instance_id": "agentscope-ai__agentscope-3978", "issue_numbers": ["3977"], "base_commit": "6047bc00f1ba0461b5833c4861cef0e050b0bfea", "patch": "diff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 1da8a78654..3820fb3a39 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -73,6 +73,7 @@ rather than constraining them with strict prompts and opinionated orchestrations\n \n ## News\n <!-- BEGIN NEWS -->\n+- **[2026-10] `FEAT`:** Voice profile management and voice cloning supported \u2014 select saved voices in chat, with DashScope and OpenAI voice cloning clients available in the Python SDK.\n - **[2026-10] `FEAT` `Experimental`:** Agent service supports realtime voice conversations over WebRTC, with text and voice sharing the same session history.\n - **[2026-09] `FEAT` `Experimental`:** SOP supported \u2014 run multi-step tasks as standard operating procedures, in both the framework and agent service. [Docs](https://docs.agentscope.io/latest/en/building-blocks/sop) | [Service](https://docs.agentscope.io/latest/en/deploy/sop)\n - **[2026-09] `FEAT`:** `TeamPipeline` supported \u2014 a leader agent delegates tasks to member agents. [Docs](https://docs.agentscope.io/latest/en/building-blocks/pipeline/team)\n@@ -82,7 +83,6 @@ rather than constraining them with strict prompts and opinionated orchestrations\n - **[2026-09] `FEAT`:** [agentscope-skill](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/skills/tree/main/skills/agentscope-skill) now supports AgentScope v2.\n - **[2026-09] `INTE`:** Support DashScope, OpenAI, Gemini and xAI realtime APIs in `RealtimeAgent`. [Example](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/tree/main/examples/realtime) | [Docs](https://docs.agentscope.io/latest/en/building-blocks/realtime/speech-to-speech)\n - **[2026-09] `FEAT` `Experimental`:** Realtime voice agent supported. [Example](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/tree/main/examples/realtime) | [Docs](https://docs.agentscope.io/latest/en/building-blocks/realtime/overview)\n-- **[2026-09] `FEAT`:** A2A protocol supported \u2014 chat with any remote A2A agent via `A2AAgent`. [Example](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/tree/main/examples/a2a) | [Docs](https://docs.agentscope.io/latest/en/building-blocks/a2a)\n <!-- END NEWS -->\n \n [More news \u2192](./docs/NEWS.md)\ndiff --git a/README_zh.md b/README_zh.md\nindex ae1d249534..0990d315a6 100644\n--- a/README_zh.md\n+++ b/README_zh.md\n@@ -72,6 +72,7 @@ AgentScope \u7684\u76ee\u6807\u662f\u5145\u5206\u53d1\u6325\u5927\u6a21\u578b\u7684\u63a8\u7406\u4e0e\u5de5\u5177\u8c03\u7528\u80fd\u529b\uff0c\n \n ## \u65b0\u95fb\n <!-- BEGIN NEWS -->\n+- **[2026-10] `\u529f\u80fd`:** \u652f\u6301\u97f3\u8272\u914d\u7f6e\u7ba1\u7406\u4e0e\u8bed\u97f3\u590d\u523b\uff0c\u53ef\u5728\u804a\u5929\u4e2d\u9009\u62e9\u5df2\u4fdd\u5b58\u7684\u97f3\u8272\uff1bPython SDK \u65b0\u589e DashScope \u548c OpenAI \u97f3\u8272\u590d\u523b\u5ba2\u6237\u7aef\u3002\n - **[2026-10] `\u529f\u80fd` `\u5b9e\u9a8c\u6027`:** \u667a\u80fd\u4f53\u670d\u52a1\u652f\u6301\u57fa\u4e8e WebRTC \u7684\u5b9e\u65f6\u8bed\u97f3\u5bf9\u8bdd\uff0c\u6587\u672c\u4e0e\u8bed\u97f3\u6a21\u5f0f\u5171\u4eab\u540c\u4e00\u4f1a\u8bdd\u5386\u53f2\u3002\n - **[2026-09] `\u529f\u80fd` `\u5b9e\u9a8c\u6027`:** \u652f\u6301 SOP\uff08\u6807\u51c6\u4f5c\u4e1a\u6d41\u7a0b\uff09\u2014\u2014 \u5c06\u591a\u6b65\u9aa4\u4efb\u52a1\u6309\u6807\u51c6\u6d41\u7a0b\u6267\u884c\uff0c\u6846\u67b6\u4e0e\u667a\u80fd\u4f53\u670d\u52a1\u5747\u5df2\u652f\u6301\u3002[\u6587\u6863](https://docs.agentscope.io/latest/zh/building-blocks/sop) | [\u670d\u52a1](https://docs.agentscope.io/latest/zh/deploy/sop)\n - **[2026-09] `\u529f\u80fd`:** \u652f\u6301 `TeamPipeline` \u2014\u2014 \u7531 leader \u667a\u80fd\u4f53\u5411\u6210\u5458\u667a\u80fd\u4f53\u5206\u6d3e\u4efb\u52a1\u3002[\u6587\u6863](https://docs.agentscope.io/latest/zh/building-blocks/pipeline/team)\n@@ -81,7 +82,6 @@ AgentScope \u7684\u76ee\u6807\u662f\u5145\u5206\u53d1\u6325\u5927\u6a21\u578b\u7684\u63a8\u7406\u4e0e\u5de5\u5177\u8c03\u7528\u80fd\u529b\uff0c\n - **[2026-09] `\u529f\u80fd`:** [agentscope-skill](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/skills/tree/main/skills/agentscope-skill) \u5df2\u9002\u914d AgentScope v2\u3002\n - **[2026-09] `\u96c6\u6210`:** `RealtimeAgent` \u652f\u6301 DashScope\u3001OpenAI\u3001Gemini \u4e0e xAI \u7684\u5b9e\u65f6\u8bed\u97f3 API\u3002[\u6837\u4f8b](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/tree/main/examples/realtime) | [\u6587\u6863](https://docs.agentscope.io/latest/zh/building-blocks/realtime/speech-to-speech)\n - **[2026-09] `\u529f\u80fd` `\u5b9e\u9a8c\u6027`:** \u652f\u6301\u5b9e\u65f6\u8bed\u97f3\u667a\u80fd\u4f53\u3002[\u6837\u4f8b](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/tree/main/examples/realtime) | [\u6587\u6863](https://docs.agentscope.io/latest/zh/building-blocks/realtime/overview)\n-- **[2026-09] `\u529f\u80fd`:** \u652f\u6301 A2A \u534f\u8bae \u2014\u2014 \u901a\u8fc7 `A2AAgent` \u4e0e\u4efb\u610f\u8fdc\u7aef A2A \u667a\u80fd\u4f53\u5bf9\u8bdd\u3002[\u6837\u4f8b](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/tree/main/examples/a2a) | [\u6587\u6863](https://docs.agentscope.io/latest/zh/building-blocks/a2a)\n <!-- END NEWS -->\n \n [\u66f4\u591a\u65b0\u95fb \u2192](./docs/NEWS_zh.md)\n", "test_patch": "", "problem_statement": "docs: README NEWS sections are one sync behind docs/NEWS.md\n## Summary\n\nThe NEWS blocks in `README.md` and `README_zh.md` (between `<!-- BEGIN NEWS -->` and `<!-- END NEWS -->`) are one item behind `docs/NEWS.md` / `docs/NEWS_zh.md` on current `main`.\n\nPR #2162 (2026-10-30, voice-profile management) prepended a new `[2026-10]` item to `docs/NEWS.md` and `docs/NEWS_zh.md` but did not sync the two READMEs (last synced 2026-10-08 in #2570). `.github/workflows/update_news.yml` sets `branches-ignore: [main]`, so a direct-to-main edit of `docs/NEWS.md` never triggers the auto-sync.\n\n## Current drift\n\n- `README.md` is missing the newest item (`[2026-10]` voice profile management / voice cloning) and still lists the `[2026-09]` A2A item, which has slid out of the top-10 window that `.github/scripts/update_news.py` maintains.\n- `README_zh.md` has the same one-item drift against `docs/NEWS_zh.md`.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nRun the repository's own sync script (`.github/scripts/update_news.py`) to regenerate both README NEWS blocks (one line in / one line out per file). Separately, it may be worth letting the workflow run on `main` too, or adding a scheduled drift check, so future direct-to-main edits can't reintroduce this.\n\nI have a small PR ready for the README re-sync and will link it here. (Prepared with the help of an AI coding assistant; verified with the repo's own script.)\n\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-11-12T17:22:48Z"}
{"repo": "agentscope-ai/agentscope", "pull_number": 3976, "instance_id": "agentscope-ai__agentscope-3976", "issue_numbers": ["3975"], "base_commit": "6047bc00f1ba0461b5833c4861cef0e050b0bfea", "patch": "diff --git a/src/agentscope/middleware/_rag.py b/src/agentscope/middleware/_rag.py\nindex 63d91f9bc4..469c0ba5eb 100644\n--- a/src/agentscope/middleware/_rag.py\n+++ b/src/agentscope/middleware/_rag.py\n@@ -362,10 +362,16 @@ async def _search_across(\n     Each knowledge base handles its own filtering \u2014 it silently drops\n     :class:`DataBlock` inputs when its embedding model is not\n     multimodal \u2014 so callers can pass the same query list to every\n-    knowledge base without per-KB pre-filtering.  Per-KB hits are\n-    flattened, sorted by descending score, and truncated to ``top_k``.\n-    With a ``rerank_model``, retrieval widens to ``rerank_candidate_k`` hits\n-    and :func:`_rerank_results` picks the final ``top_k`` out of them.\n+    knowledge base without per-KB pre-filtering.  That filtering is\n+    best-effort: a multimodal model can still reject a block it does\n+    not accept, and a knowledge base can fail for unrelated reasons\n+    (unavailable embedding provider or vector store).  A failing\n+    knowledge base is logged by name and skipped, so the others still\n+    contribute; if none of them has a hit, the first error propagates\n+    instead.  Per-KB hits are flattened, sorted by descending\n+    score, and truncated to ``top_k``.  With a ``rerank_model``,\n+    retrieval widens to ``rerank_candidate_k`` hits and\n+    :func:`_rerank_results` picks the final ``top_k`` out of them.\n     Rerank is best-effort \u2014 a failing model keeps the vector order.\n \n     .. note::\n@@ -411,18 +417,49 @@ async def _search_across(\n         rerank_candidate_k = top_k\n \n     queries_list = list(queries)\n-    per_kb = await asyncio.gather(\n-        *(\n-            kb.search(\n+\n+    async def _search_one(\n+        kb: \"KnowledgeBase\",\n+    ) -> list[\"VectorSearchResult\"] | Exception:\n+        \"\"\"Turn a per-KB failure into a value so the others still merge.\"\"\"\n+        try:\n+            return await kb.search(\n                 queries=queries_list,\n                 top_k=rerank_candidate_k,\n                 score_threshold=score_threshold,\n             )\n-            for kb in knowledge_bases\n-        ),\n-    )\n+        except Exception as error:\n+            return error\n+\n+    # One knowledge base must not erase the others' context.  Only\n+    # ordinary exceptions are collected: ``CancelledError`` is a\n+    # ``BaseException`` and stays uncaught so ``gather`` re-raises it at\n+    # once instead of waiting for a slow sibling to finish.\n+    per_kb = await asyncio.gather(*(_search_one(kb) for kb in knowledge_bases))\n+\n+    failures: list[tuple[\"KnowledgeBase\", Exception]] = []\n+    successful: list[list[\"VectorSearchResult\"]] = []\n+    for kb, hits in zip(knowledge_bases, per_kb):\n+        if isinstance(hits, Exception):\n+            failures.append((kb, hits))\n+        else:\n+            successful.append(hits)\n+\n+    merged = [r for sub in successful for r in sub]\n+    if failures and not merged:\n+        # Nothing else to show, so report the failure instead of\n+        # \"No relevant content found.\"  The caller logs it.\n+        raise failures[0][1]\n+\n+    # Only the knowledge bases that are really skipped get a warning;\n+    # one that left nothing to merge was re-raised above.\n+    for kb, error in failures:\n+        logger.warning(\n+            \"Knowledge base %r search failed; skipping it.\",\n+            kb.name,\n+            exc_info=error,\n+        )\n \n-    merged = [r for sub in per_kb for r in sub]\n     merged.sort(key=lambda r: r.score, reverse=True)\n     results = merged[:rerank_candidate_k]\n     if rerank_model is None or not results:\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/tests/middleware_rag_test.py b/tests/middleware_rag_test.py\nindex 7eed186306..b1c941c9ca 100644\n--- a/tests/middleware_rag_test.py\n+++ b/tests/middleware_rag_test.py\n@@ -129,9 +129,17 @@ class _StubKnowledgeBase:\n     name = \"stub-kb\"\n     description = \"Stub knowledge base.\"\n \n-    def __init__(self, results: list[VectorSearchResult]) -> None:\n+    def __init__(\n+        self,\n+        results: list[VectorSearchResult],\n+        error: BaseException | None = None,\n+        name: str | None = None,\n+    ) -> None:\n         self.results = results\n+        self.error = error\n         self.search_calls: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n+        if name is not None:\n+            self.name = name\n \n     async def search(\n         self,\n@@ -147,6 +155,8 @@ async def search(\n                 \"score_threshold\": score_threshold,\n             },\n         )\n+        if self.error is not None:\n+            raise self.error\n         return self.results[:top_k]\n \n \n@@ -1207,6 +1217,157 @@ async def test_rerank_model_failure_keeps_vector_order(self) -> None:\n         )\n \n \n+class SearchAcrossFailureIsolation(IsolatedAsyncioTestCase):\n+    \"\"\"A failing knowledge base must not drop the others' context.\"\"\"\n+\n+    async def test_failing_kb_does_not_drop_the_others(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"The working knowledge base still returns its hits.\"\"\"\n+        failing = _StubKnowledgeBase(\n+            [],\n+            error=ValueError(\"Unsupported media type 'application/pdf'\"),\n+            name=\"catalog\",\n+        )\n+        with self.assertLogs(\"as\", level=\"WARNING\") as captured:\n+            results = await _search_across(\n+                [\n+                    _StubKnowledgeBase(\n+                        [\n+                            _make_result(\n+                                \"Returns within 30 days.\",\n+                                \"doc-1\",\n+                                0.8,\n+                            ),\n+                        ],\n+                        name=\"policies\",\n+                    ),\n+                    failing,\n+                ],\n+                [\"How long do I have to return this order?\"],\n+                top_k=2,\n+                score_threshold=None,\n+            )\n+\n+        self.assertListEqual(\n+            [result.document_id for result in results],\n+            [\"doc-1\"],\n+        )\n+        # The skipped knowledge base is named, so an operator can tell\n+        # which one to look at without correlating stack traces.\n+        self.assertIn(\"catalog\", captured.records[0].getMessage())\n+\n+    async def test_all_knowledge_bases_failing_raises(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"With nothing left to merge, the error still surfaces.\"\"\"\n+        with self.assertRaisesRegex(ValueError, \"unavailable\"):\n+            await _search_across(\n+                [\n+                    _StubKnowledgeBase(\n+                        [],\n+                        error=ValueError(\"provider unavailable\"),\n+                        name=\"policies\",\n+                    ),\n+                    _StubKnowledgeBase(\n+                        [],\n+                        error=ValueError(\"provider unavailable\"),\n+                        name=\"catalog\",\n+                    ),\n+                ],\n+                [\"Where is Paris?\"],\n+                top_k=2,\n+                score_threshold=None,\n+            )\n+\n+    async def test_cancelled_reply_is_not_swallowed(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Cancellation is not a per-KB scoring problem.\"\"\"\n+        with self.assertRaises(asyncio.CancelledError):\n+            await _search_across(\n+                [\n+                    _StubKnowledgeBase(\n+                        [_make_result(\"Paris is in France.\", \"doc-1\", 0.8)],\n+                        name=\"policies\",\n+                    ),\n+                    _StubKnowledgeBase(\n+                        [],\n+                        error=asyncio.CancelledError(),\n+                        name=\"catalog\",\n+                    ),\n+                ],\n+                [\"Where is Paris?\"],\n+                top_k=2,\n+                score_threshold=None,\n+            )\n+\n+    async def test_cancellation_reaches_the_caller_while_a_sibling_blocks(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"A cancelled search propagates without waiting for a stalled\n+        sibling: the caller must see the cancellation before the other\n+        knowledge base is released.\"\"\"\n+        blocked_started = asyncio.Event()\n+        blocked_released = asyncio.Event()\n+\n+        class _BlockingKnowledgeBase(_StubKnowledgeBase):\n+            async def search(\n+                self,\n+                queries: list[str | TextBlock | DataBlock],\n+                top_k: int = 5,\n+                score_threshold: float | None = None,\n+            ) -> list[VectorSearchResult]:\n+                blocked_started.set()\n+                await blocked_released.wait()\n+                return self.results\n+\n+        cancelled = _StubKnowledgeBase(\n+            [],\n+            error=asyncio.CancelledError(),\n+            name=\"catalog\",\n+        )\n+        blocking = _BlockingKnowledgeBase([], name=\"policies\")\n+\n+        search_task = asyncio.ensure_future(\n+            _search_across(\n+                [blocking, cancelled],\n+                [\"Where is Paris?\"],\n+                top_k=2,\n+                score_threshold=None,\n+            ),\n+        )\n+        await asyncio.wait_for(blocked_started.wait(), timeout=2)\n+        try:\n+            # The blocked search is still running, so this only returns\n+            # if the sibling's own cancellation was propagated at once.\n+            await asyncio.wait_for(\n+                asyncio.shield(search_task),\n+                timeout=2,\n+            )\n+            self.fail(\"the cancellation was swallowed\")\n+        except asyncio.CancelledError:\n+            pass\n+        finally:\n+            # Releasing the sibling afterwards must not resurrect the\n+            # turn or raise an unhandled exception of its own.\n+            blocked_released.set()\n+            await asyncio.gather(search_task, return_exceptions=True)\n+            self.assertTrue(search_task.done())\n+\n+    async def test_failure_is_not_reported_as_no_hits(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"If the knowledge bases that worked found nothing, the error\n+        still surfaces instead of an empty result.\"\"\"\n+        with self.assertRaisesRegex(RuntimeError, \"unavailable\"):\n+            await _search_across(\n+                [\n+                    _StubKnowledgeBase([], name=\"policies\"),\n+                    _StubKnowledgeBase(\n+                        [],\n+                        error=RuntimeError(\"embedding provider unavailable\"),\n+                        name=\"catalog\",\n+                    ),\n+                ],\n+                [\"Where is Paris?\"],\n+                top_k=2,\n+                score_threshold=None,\n+            )\n+\n+\n class RAGHintTemplateValidationTest(IsolatedAsyncioTestCase):\n     \"\"\"``hint_template`` must be renderable, not merely contain a marker.\"\"\"\n \n", "problem_statement": "[Bug]: RAGMiddleware drops all knowledge-base context when one knowledge base cannot embed an attachment\n### Prerequisites\n\n- [x] I have searched the existing issues and discussions, and this is not a duplicate.\n- [x] This is a bug, not a usage question.\n\nRelated: #3649 and #3656 cover sibling vector queries inside one `KnowledgeBase.search`. This issue is about separate knowledge bases in `RAGMiddleware`. I found no issue or pull request for it.\n\n### Background / Description\n\n`RAGMiddleware` takes several knowledge bases, and they may use different embedding models ([source](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/blob/6047bc00f1ba0461b5833c4861cef0e050b0bfea/src/agentscope/middleware/_rag.py#L4-L8)). In static mode it searches all of them with the user's turn, attachments included. `_search_across` relies on each knowledge base to drop the inputs its model cannot use ([source](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/blob/6047bc00f1ba0461b5833c4861cef0e050b0bfea/src/agentscope/middleware/_rag.py#L362-L365)), but `KnowledgeBase.search` drops `DataBlock`s only for text-only models ([source](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/blob/6047bc00f1ba0461b5833c4861cef0e050b0bfea/src/agentscope/rag/_knowledge.py#L246-L249)). A multimodal model can still reject a block. For example, `DashScopeEmbeddingModel` raises `ValueError` while building the request for any media type other than `image/*` or `video/*`, such as a PDF ([source](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/blob/6047bc00f1ba0461b5833c4861cef0e050b0bfea/src/agentscope/embedding/_dashscope/_model.py#L547-L550)).\n\n`_search_across` gathers the per-knowledge-base searches without isolating failures ([source](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/blob/6047bc00f1ba0461b5833c4861cef0e050b0bfea/src/agentscope/middleware/_rag.py#L414-L423)), so that one `ValueError` aborts the whole search. The static-mode handler then logs it and continues without any context ([source](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/blob/6047bc00f1ba0461b5833c4861cef0e050b0bfea/src/agentscope/middleware/_rag.py#L990-L995)). A text knowledge base that matched the question contributes nothing either.\n\nFor example, take a support agent with a text knowledge base of store policies and an image knowledge base of product photos. A customer attaches an invoice PDF and asks about returns. The agent answers without the return policy, and the only trace is an ERROR log line. The same coupling applies when one knowledge base fails for any other reason, such as an unavailable embedding provider or vector store. In agentic mode the queries are text only, but there too one failing knowledge base makes the `search_knowledge` tool return `Search failed: ...` instead of the other knowledge bases' hits ([source](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/blob/6047bc00f1ba0461b5833c4861cef0e050b0bfea/src/agentscope/middleware/_rag.py#L323-L329)).\n\nExpected behavior: a knowledge base whose search fails is logged and skipped, and the others still contribute, much as a failing reranker already falls back to the vector order ([source](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/blob/6047bc00f1ba0461b5833c4861cef0e050b0bfea/src/agentscope/middleware/_rag.py#L369)). When every knowledge base fails, the current behavior can stay.\n\n### Error Messages / Observed Behavior\n\nThe reproduction below prints:\n\n```text\npolicies         : 1 hint(s), has the return policy: True\npolicies+catalog : 0 hint(s), has the return policy: False\ncatalog.search   : ValueError: Unsupported media type 'application/pdf' in DataBlock. Expected image/* or video/*.\nDashScope API calls: 0\n```\n\nThe first line is the control: the same message with only the text knowledge base. In the second run the middleware logs:\n\n```text\nERROR   | _rag:on_reasoning:991 - Knowledge-base search failed; proceeding without matched context.\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  ...\nValueError: Unsupported media type 'application/pdf' in DataBlock. Expected image/* or video/*.\n```\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Save this as `repro_rag_kb_failure.py`:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"RAGMiddleware static mode: one knowledge base that cannot embed an\nattachment drops the context of every knowledge base.\n\nRuns offline: the DashScope multimodal model rejects the PDF block while\nbuilding the request, before any API call.\n\"\"\"\nimport asyncio\nfrom types import SimpleNamespace\n\nimport dashscope\n\nfrom agentscope.credential import DashScopeCredential\nfrom agentscope.embedding import DashScopeEmbeddingModel, EmbeddingResponse\nfrom agentscope.message import (\n    Base64Source,\n    DataBlock,\n    HintBlock,\n    Msg,\n    TextBlock,\n)\nfrom agentscope.middleware import RAGMiddleware\nfrom agentscope.rag import Chunk, KnowledgeBase, QdrantStore, VectorRecord\n\napi_calls = []\ndashscope.MultiModalEmbedding.call = lambda **kw: api_calls.append(kw)\n\n\nclass TextEmbedding:\n    \"\"\"Offline stand-in for a text-only embedding model.\"\"\"\n\n    supports_multimodal = False\n    dimensions = 3\n\n    async def __call__(self, inputs):\n        return EmbeddingResponse(embeddings=[[1.0, 0.0, 0.0]] * len(inputs))\n\n\nasync def hints_seen(knowledge_bases, msg):\n    \"\"\"Run one static-mode reply; return the hints the model would see.\"\"\"\n    middleware = RAGMiddleware(\n        knowledge_bases=knowledge_bases,\n        parameters=RAGMiddleware.Parameters(mode=\"static\"),\n    )\n    context, seen = [], []\n\n    def append_context(name, blocks):\n        carrier = Msg(name=name, role=\"assistant\", content=blocks)\n        carrier.id = \"reply-1\"\n        context.append(carrier)\n\n    state = SimpleNamespace(context=context, reply_id=\"reply-1\",\n                            session_id=\"s-1\", cur_iter=0,\n                            append_context=append_context)\n    agent = SimpleNamespace(name=\"assistant\", state=state)\n\n    async def reasoning(**_):\n        seen.extend(b.hint for m in context for b in m.content\n                    if isinstance(b, HintBlock))\n        yield \"reasoning\"\n\n    async def reply(**_):\n        async for evt in middleware.on_reasoning(\n            agent=agent, input_kwargs={}, next_handler=reasoning,\n        ):\n            yield evt\n\n    async for _ in middleware.on_reply(\n        agent=agent, input_kwargs={\"inputs\": msg}, next_handler=reply,\n    ):\n        pass\n    return seen\n\n\nasync def main():\n    async with QdrantStore(location=\":memory:\") as store:\n        await store.create_collection(\"policies\", dimensions=3)\n        await store.insert(\"policies\", [VectorRecord(\n            vector=[1.0, 0.0, 0.0],\n            document_id=\"returns\",\n            chunk=Chunk(\n                content=TextBlock(text=\"Items can be returned within 30 days.\"),\n                source=\"returns.md\", chunk_index=0, total_chunks=1,\n            ),\n        )])\n        policies = KnowledgeBase(\n            name=\"policies\", description=\"Store policies.\",\n            embedding_model=TextEmbedding(),\n            vector_store=store, collection=\"policies\",\n        )\n        catalog = KnowledgeBase(\n            name=\"catalog\", description=\"Product photos.\",\n            embedding_model=DashScopeEmbeddingModel(\n                credential=DashScopeCredential(api_key=\"sk-offline\"),\n                model=\"multimodal-embedding-v1\", dimensions=1024,\n            ),\n            vector_store=store, collection=\"catalog\",\n        )\n        question = TextBlock(text=\"How long do I have to return this order?\")\n        invoice = DataBlock(source=Base64Source(\n            media_type=\"application/pdf\", data=\"JVBERi0xLjQK\",\n        ))\n        msg = Msg(name=\"user\", role=\"user\", content=[question, invoice])\n\n        for kbs in ([policies], [policies, catalog]):\n            hints = await hints_seen(kbs, msg)\n            print(f\"{'+'.join(kb.name for kb in kbs):<17}: \"\n                  f\"{len(hints)} hint(s), \"\n                  f\"has the return policy: {any('30 days' in h for h in hints)}\")\n        try:\n            await catalog.search([question, invoice])\n        except ValueError as e:\n            print(f\"catalog.search   : ValueError: {e}\")\n        print(f\"DashScope API calls: {len(api_calls)}\")\n\n\nasyncio.run(main())\n```\n\n2. From a checkout of main at `6047bc00f1ba0461b5833c4861cef0e050b0bfea` (`2.0.12dev`), run:\n\n```bash\npython -m pip install -e \".[vdb-qdrant]\"\npython repro_rag_kb_failure.py\n```\n\nNo network access or credentials are needed. The API key is a placeholder, and the script replaces the DashScope SDK call with a counter, which stays at 0.\n\n### Environment\n\n- AgentScope: `2.0.12dev`, main commit `6047bc00f1ba0461b5833c4861cef0e050b0bfea`.\n- Python: 3.11.9, with qdrant-client 1.19.1 and dashscope 1.27.7.\n- OS: Windows.\n\n### Proposed Scope\n\nWould it fit for `_search_across` to gather with `return_exceptions=True`, log each failing knowledge base by name, merge the others' results, and re-raise only when every knowledge base failed? `CancelledError` and other non-`Exception` errors would still propagate. Both modes share the helper, so agentic mode would then return the working knowledge bases' hits. If you would rather the tool result also name the skipped ones, I can add that. I can add regression tests for a failing knowledge base next to a working one, both in `_search_across` and through static mode, and for the case where all of them fail.\n\nA single multimodal knowledge base would still lose the text part of such a turn, because all inputs go into one embedding call. Skipping blocks outside the model card's `input_types` could address that, but it needs a new capability check on the embedding model, so I would leave it out of this issue.\n\nClaude Code assisted with source inspection, duplicate searches, and the offline reproduction. I have not started a fix.\n\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-11-12T16:55:24Z"}
{"repo": "agentscope-ai/agentscope", "pull_number": 3966, "instance_id": "agentscope-ai__agentscope-3966", "issue_numbers": ["3964"], "base_commit": "3fef100ee13d70905723d0000608bcce2d7e4a0d", "patch": "diff --git a/src/agentscope/app/workspace_manager/_docker_workspace_manager.py b/src/agentscope/app/workspace_manager/_docker_workspace_manager.py\nindex 79323441bc..4904b23456 100644\n--- a/src/agentscope/app/workspace_manager/_docker_workspace_manager.py\n+++ b/src/agentscope/app/workspace_manager/_docker_workspace_manager.py\n@@ -179,7 +179,7 @@ def _workdir_for(\n         \"\"\"\n         root = os.path.realpath(self._basedir)\n         workdir = os.path.realpath(os.path.join(root, workspace_id))\n-        if not workdir.startswith(root + os.sep):\n+        if not self._is_strictly_inside(root, workdir):\n             raise ValueError(\n                 f\"workspace_id {workspace_id!r} escapes the workspace \"\n                 f\"base directory\",\n@@ -194,10 +194,43 @@ def _workdir_for(\n         # ``basedir`` are declined rather than rejected, leaving the\n         # caller with an ordinary empty workspace.\n         legacy = os.path.realpath(os.path.join(root, user_id, agent_id))\n-        if legacy.startswith(root + os.sep) and os.path.isdir(legacy):\n+        if self._is_strictly_inside(root, legacy) and os.path.isdir(legacy):\n             return legacy\n         return workdir\n \n+    @staticmethod\n+    def _is_strictly_inside(root: str, path: str) -> bool:\n+        \"\"\"Whether ``path`` is an entry strictly below ``root``.\n+\n+        ``path.startswith(root + os.sep)`` cannot decide this: when\n+        ``root`` is a filesystem root the separator doubles (``\"/\"``\n+        becomes ``\"//\"`` and ``\"D:\\\\\"`` becomes ``\"D:\\\\\\\\\"``), so no path\n+        ever matches and every workspace id is rejected. The relative\n+        path carries the same relation and stays valid for every root.\n+\n+        Args:\n+            root (`str`):\n+                The absolute, resolved directory expected to contain\n+                ``path``.\n+            path (`str`):\n+                The absolute, resolved candidate entry.\n+\n+        Returns:\n+            `bool`:\n+                `True` if ``path`` lies below ``root`` rather than at or\n+                above it.\n+        \"\"\"\n+        try:\n+            relative = os.path.relpath(path, root)\n+        except ValueError:\n+            # Different drives on Windows: nothing is below the root.\n+            return False\n+        return (\n+            relative != os.curdir\n+            and relative != os.pardir\n+            and not relative.startswith(os.pardir + os.sep)\n+        )\n+\n     # \u2500\u2500 workspace construction \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n \n     async def _build_and_start(\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/tests/workspace_manager_docker_test.py b/tests/workspace_manager_docker_test.py\nindex 8e6fb62fe7..2c8c825904 100644\n--- a/tests/workspace_manager_docker_test.py\n+++ b/tests/workspace_manager_docker_test.py\n@@ -138,6 +138,25 @@ async def test_workspace_id_cannot_escape_the_basedir(self) -> None:\n             with self.assertRaises(ValueError):\n                 manager._workdir_for(workspace_id)\n \n+    async def test_filesystem_root_basedir_still_contains_workdirs(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"A basedir at a filesystem root contains every ordinary id.\n+\n+        Appending a separator to a root yields ``\"//\"`` on POSIX and\n+        ``\"C:\\\\\\\\\"`` on Windows, so the old prefix test matched nothing\n+        and rejected every id with a message claiming it escaped the\n+        base directory.\n+        \"\"\"\n+        root = os.path.realpath(os.sep)\n+        manager = DockerWorkspaceManager(root)\n+\n+        for workspace_id in (\"ws-normal\", \"abc123\"):\n+            self.assertEqual(\n+                manager._workdir_for(workspace_id),\n+                os.path.join(root, workspace_id),\n+            )\n+\n     async def test_legacy_workdir_is_kept_mounted(self) -> None:\n         \"\"\"A pre-existing <basedir>/<user>/<agent> keeps being used.\"\"\"\n         legacy = os.path.join(self.basedir, \"u1\", \"a1\")\n", "problem_statement": "[Bug]: a Docker workspace basedir at a filesystem root rejects every workspace id\n### Prerequisites\n\n- [x] I have searched the existing [issues](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/issues) and [discussions](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/discussions), and this is not a duplicate. The closest is #3728, the same defect class in `tool/_base.py`, fixed by #3719.\n- [x] This is a bug, not a usage question.\n\n### Background / Description\n\n`DockerWorkspaceManager._workdir_for` decides whether the bind-mounted host directory stays inside `basedir` by appending a separator to the base:\n\n```python\nroot = os.path.realpath(self._basedir)\nworkdir = os.path.realpath(os.path.join(root, workspace_id))\nif not workdir.startswith(root + os.sep):\n    raise ValueError(\n        f\"workspace_id {workspace_id!r} escapes the workspace base directory\",\n    )\n```\n\nFor a filesystem root the prefix is not a valid path prefix: `\"/\"` becomes `\"//\"`, and `\"D:\\\\\"` becomes `\"D:\\\\\\\\\"` (a raw backslash is escaped once more by the separator), so `str.startswith` can never match:\n\n```python\n>>> os.path.realpath(os.sep) + os.sep      # \"//\" on POSIX, \"C:\\\\\" + \"\\\\\" on Windows\n'//'\n>>> \"/ws-normal\".startswith(\"//\")\nFalse\n```\n\nThis is the defect #3728 reported for the working-directory containment check and #3719 fixed in `tool/_base.py` two days ago. The consequence here is stronger, because this check is a rejection gate rather than an auto-allow: **every** workspace id raises `ValueError`, although nothing escapes the base directory. A manager configured with `/` (the app running inside a container whose workspace root is the filesystem root) or a Windows drive root cannot create a single workspace, and the error claims the id is a traversal attempt when it is an ordinary name.\n\nThe docstring states the intent precisely \u2014 \"a value that escapes `basedir` would hand the container the host filesystem. Anything not landing strictly inside is rejected\" \u2014 so an id that does land inside should be accepted.\n\nThe sibling `BubblewrapWorkspaceManager._workdir_for` applies the same rule with `os.path.commonpath`, which handles the root case correctly; only the Docker manager kept the prefix test.\n\n### Error Messages\n\n```shell\n$ python -c \"\nfrom agentscope.app.workspace_manager import DockerWorkspaceManager\nimport os\nm = DockerWorkspaceManager(basedir=os.path.abspath(os.sep))\nm._workdir_for('ws-normal')\n\"\nValueError: workspace_id 'ws-normal' escapes the workspace base directory\n```\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\nWindows 11 / Python 3.13, and identically on POSIX with `basedir=\"/\"`:\n\n```python\nimport os\n\nfrom agentscope.app.workspace_manager import DockerWorkspaceManager\n\nmanager = DockerWorkspaceManager(basedir=os.path.abspath(os.sep))\nprint(os.path.realpath(manager._basedir))   # 'C:\\\\'\nmanager._workdir_for(\"ws-normal\")\n```\n\nExpected: `\"C:\\\\ws-normal\"` (or `\"/ws-normal\"` on POSIX), which is inside the base directory.\nActual: `ValueError: workspace_id 'ws-normal' escapes the workspace base directory`, raised before any container work, so `create_workspace` / `get_workspace` fail for every id.\n\nThe same prefix test is used by the legacy-dir fallback at line 197, so a `<basedir>/<user>/<agent>` directory under such a base is declined as well.\n\n### Where it lives\n\n- `src/agentscope/app/workspace_manager/_docker_workspace_manager.py:182` \u2014 the workspace id\n- `src/agentscope/app/workspace_manager/_docker_workspace_manager.py:197` \u2014 the legacy layout fallback\n\n### Proposed fix\n\nDecide containment with `os.path.relpath(workdir, root)` exactly as #3719 does (a relative path equal to `os.pardir` or starting with `os.pardir + os.sep` escapes), or with `os.path.commonpath` as `BubblewrapWorkspaceManager` already does, keeping the same `ValueError` for real escapes. Add a test that configures the filesystem root as `basedir` and expects an ordinary id to be accepted, next to the existing `test_workspace_id_cannot_escape_the_basedir`.\n\nI'd like to implement this and open a PR if the direction looks right.\n\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-11-12T03:53:31Z"}
{"repo": "agentscope-ai/agentscope", "pull_number": 3958, "instance_id": "agentscope-ai__agentscope-3958", "issue_numbers": ["3956"], "base_commit": "db780a4c341c9c79a313303b55d9428a30e365fa", "patch": "diff --git a/src/agentscope/rag/_vdb/_qdrant.py b/src/agentscope/rag/_vdb/_qdrant.py\nindex d63d7f209c..acee62b007 100644\n--- a/src/agentscope/rag/_vdb/_qdrant.py\n+++ b/src/agentscope/rag/_vdb/_qdrant.py\n@@ -313,7 +313,21 @@ async def search(\n             `list[VectorSearchResult]`:\n                 Results ordered by descending similarity score.\n         \"\"\"\n-        response = await self.get_client().query_points(\n+        from qdrant_client import models\n+\n+        client = self.get_client()\n+        collection_info = await client.get_collection(collection)\n+        vectors = collection_info.config.params.vectors\n+        if isinstance(vectors, dict):\n+            vectors = vectors.get(\"\")\n+        if not isinstance(vectors, models.VectorParams):\n+            raise ValueError(\n+                \"QdrantStore.search requires an unnamed dense vector.\",\n+            )\n+        # The constructor's metric only applies to newly created collections.\n+        # Read the actual schema, including after an external recreation.\n+        distance = vectors.distance\n+        response = await client.query_points(\n             collection_name=collection,\n             query=query_vector,\n             limit=top_k,\n@@ -322,7 +336,11 @@ async def search(\n         )\n         # ``Euclid`` / ``Manhattan`` are distances, so negate them to\n         # keep ``score`` higher-is-better like ``Cosine`` / ``Dot``.\n-        sign = -1 if self._distance in (\"Euclid\", \"Manhattan\") else 1\n+        sign = (\n+            -1\n+            if distance in (models.Distance.EUCLID, models.Distance.MANHATTAN)\n+            else 1\n+        )\n         return [\n             VectorSearchResult(\n                 score=sign * point.score,\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/tests/rag_vdb_qdrant_test.py b/tests/rag_vdb_qdrant_test.py\nindex 698bb259ef..f90e1e4634 100644\n--- a/tests/rag_vdb_qdrant_test.py\n+++ b/tests/rag_vdb_qdrant_test.py\n@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@\n \"\"\"Unit tests for the QdrantStore class.\"\"\"\n from contextlib import AsyncExitStack\n from importlib.util import find_spec\n+from tempfile import TemporaryDirectory\n from types import SimpleNamespace\n from unittest import skipUnless\n from unittest.async_case import IsolatedAsyncioTestCase\n@@ -94,6 +95,130 @@ def _make_record(\n     )\n \n \n+class QdrantMetricTest(IsolatedAsyncioTestCase):\n+    \"\"\"Real collection metadata determines search score semantics.\"\"\"\n+\n+    async def asyncSetUp(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Create an in-memory Qdrant store before each test.\"\"\"\n+        self._exit_stack = AsyncExitStack()\n+        self.store = await self._exit_stack.enter_async_context(\n+            QdrantStore(location=\":memory:\"),\n+        )\n+\n+    async def asyncTearDown(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Close the store after each test.\"\"\"\n+        await self._exit_stack.aclose()\n+\n+    async def test_existing_collection_metric_controls_ranking(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Reopened collections retain distance ranking and thresholds.\"\"\"\n+\n+        class QueryEmbedding:\n+            \"\"\"Return the fixed query vector without a model service.\"\"\"\n+\n+            dimensions = 3\n+            supports_multimodal = False\n+\n+            async def __call__(self, queries: list) -> SimpleNamespace:\n+                return SimpleNamespace(\n+                    embeddings=[[1.0, 0.0, 0.0] for _ in queries],\n+                )\n+\n+        for metric in (\"Euclid\", \"Manhattan\"):\n+            with self.subTest(metric=metric), TemporaryDirectory() as path:\n+                async with QdrantStore(path=path, distance=metric) as writer:\n+                    await writer.create_collection(\"existing\", dimensions=3)\n+                    await writer.insert(\n+                        \"existing\",\n+                        [\n+                            _make_record(name, [value, 0.0, 0.0], name)\n+                            for name, value in (\n+                                (\"exact\", 1.0),\n+                                (\"near\", 2.0),\n+                                (\"far\", 11.0),\n+                            )\n+                        ],\n+                    )\n+                # The default is a creation option, not the existing metric.\n+                async with QdrantStore(path=path) as reader:\n+                    kb = KnowledgeBase(\n+                        name=\"existing\",\n+                        description=\"Existing distance collection\",\n+                        embedding_model=QueryEmbedding(),\n+                        vector_store=reader,\n+                        collection=\"existing\",\n+                    )\n+                    hits = await kb.search([\"query\"], top_k=3)\n+                    self.assertEqual(\n+                        [(hit.document_id, hit.score) for hit in hits],\n+                        [(\"exact\", 0.0), (\"near\", -1.0), (\"far\", -10.0)],\n+                    )\n+                    filtered = await kb.search(\n+                        [\"query\"],\n+                        top_k=3,\n+                        score_threshold=-1.0,\n+                    )\n+                    self.assertEqual(\n+                        [hit.document_id for hit in filtered],\n+                        [\"exact\", \"near\"],\n+                    )\n+\n+    async def test_metric_tracks_external_collection_recreation(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"A live store does not retain a deleted collection's old metric.\"\"\"\n+        from qdrant_client import models\n+\n+        client = self.store.get_client()\n+        for metric, expected in ((\"Euclid\", -1.0), (\"Dot\", 2.0)):\n+            with self.subTest(metric=metric):\n+                await client.create_collection(\n+                    \"recreated\",\n+                    vectors_config=models.VectorParams(\n+                        size=3,\n+                        distance=metric,\n+                    ),\n+                )\n+                try:\n+                    await self.store.insert(\n+                        \"recreated\",\n+                        [_make_record(\"near\", [2.0, 0.0, 0.0], \"near\")],\n+                    )\n+                    hits = await self.store.search(\n+                        \"recreated\",\n+                        [1.0, 0.0, 0.0],\n+                    )\n+                    self.assertEqual(hits[0].score, expected)\n+                finally:\n+                    await client.delete_collection(\"recreated\")\n+\n+    async def test_default_dense_vector_in_named_config(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"The empty vector name is Qdrant's default query target.\"\"\"\n+        from qdrant_client import models\n+\n+        client = self.store.get_client()\n+        await client.create_collection(\n+            \"default-named\",\n+            vectors_config={\n+                \"\": models.VectorParams(size=3, distance=\"Euclid\"),\n+                \"named\": models.VectorParams(size=3, distance=\"Dot\"),\n+            },\n+        )\n+        record = _make_record(\"near\", [2.0, 0.0, 0.0], \"near\")\n+        await client.upsert(\n+            \"default-named\",\n+            points=[\n+                models.PointStruct(\n+                    id=1,\n+                    vector={\"\": record.vector},\n+                    payload={\n+                        \"document_id\": record.document_id,\n+                        \"chunk\": record.chunk.model_dump(mode=\"json\"),\n+                    },\n+                ),\n+            ],\n+        )\n+        hits = await self.store.search(\"default-named\", [1.0, 0.0, 0.0])\n+        self.assertEqual(hits[0].score, -1.0)\n+\n+\n class QdrantStoreTest(IsolatedAsyncioTestCase):\n     \"\"\"The test cases for the QdrantStore class.\"\"\"\n \n", "problem_statement": "[Bug]: Reopening Qdrant distance collections with default settings reverses retrieval ranking\n### Problem\n\nQdrantStore.search decides whether to negate a distance using the store constructor's `distance`, rather than the metric of the collection being queried. The constructor documents that option as the metric for newly created collections. Reopening an existing Euclid/Manhattan collection with the default client can therefore invert KnowledgeBase ranking and defeat its score threshold.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nVerified on main db780a4c (relevant source unchanged from f07e98a6), Python 3.12 and qdrant-client 1.20.0. This uses real Qdrant local disk persistence and deterministic query vectors, without a model service.\n\n1. Create a collection using `QdrantStore(path=path, distance=\"Euclid\")`, dimensions=2.\n2. Insert exact `[1,0]`, near `[2,0]`, and far `[11,0]`; close the store.\n3. Reopen with `QdrantStore(path=path)` and bind a KnowledgeBase whose query embedding is `[1,0]`.\n4. Search with top_k=3, including score_threshold=-1.\n\nNative Qdrant returns exact=0, near=1, far=10. KnowledgeBase with the default reader returns far=10, near=1, exact=0. The threshold incorrectly retains far. The public search_knowledge tool also renders far first. Explicitly passing distance=\"Euclid\" returns exact=0, near=-1, far=-10, and correctly excludes far at threshold=-1. top_k=1 is a healthy control because Qdrant already selects the nearest single record before adapter normalization.\n\nRelated #2482/#2486 established higher-is-better scores for distance metrics, but tested stores created and read with matching constructor configuration; existing-collection reopening remains affected.\n\n### Proposed repair\n\nRead the queried collection's actual vector metric for score normalization; retain the constructor option as the default for creation. Start without a metadata cache so an external collection recreation cannot retain an obsolete metric. Regressions should cover disk reopening, thresholds, matching configuration and multiple metrics queried through one store.\n\nAI assistance: Codex assisted inspection, deterministic reproduction and proposal.\n\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-11-11T10:47:13Z"}
{"repo": "agentscope-ai/agentscope", "pull_number": 3953, "instance_id": "agentscope-ai__agentscope-3953", "issue_numbers": ["3948"], "base_commit": "3fef100ee13d70905723d0000608bcce2d7e4a0d", "patch": "diff --git a/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/components/chat/TextInput.tsx b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/components/chat/TextInput.tsx\nindex 0e673600d5..e15e9c9453 100644\n--- a/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/components/chat/TextInput.tsx\n+++ b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/components/chat/TextInput.tsx\n@@ -198,8 +198,11 @@ export const TextInput = forwardRef<TextInputRef, TextInputProps>(\n \t\tconst textareaRef = useRef<HTMLTextAreaElement>(null);\n \t\tconst fileInputRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null);\n \t\tconst measureRef = useRef<HTMLSpanElement>(null);\n+\t\tconst ghostColumnRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\n \t\t/** ``true`` \u2014 textarea takes the full width, buttons drop to their own row. */\n \t\tconst [isStacked, setIsStacked] = useState(false);\n+\t\t/** Width of the column the ghost measures into; changes re-run both measurements. */\n+\t\tconst [composerWidth, setComposerWidth] = useState(0);\n \t\tconst asrContextRef = useRef({ key: asrResetKey, mounted: true });\n \n \t\tuseEffect(() => {\n@@ -321,7 +324,7 @@ export const TextInput = forwardRef<TextInputRef, TextInputProps>(\n \t\t\ttextarea.style.height = 'auto';\n \t\t\ttextarea.style.height = `${textarea.scrollHeight}px`;\n \t\t\t// Stacking widens the textarea, so the line count has to be redone.\n-\t\t}, [value, isStacked]);\n+\t\t}, [value, isStacked, composerWidth]);\n \n \t\t// Measured on the ghost, not the textarea: stacking widens the textarea, so\n \t\t// measuring it would flip-flop (wraps \u2192 stack \u2192 fits \u2192 unstack \u2192 wraps).\n@@ -329,7 +332,21 @@ export const TextInput = forwardRef<TextInputRef, TextInputProps>(\n \t\t\tconst ghost = measureRef.current;\n \t\t\tif (!ghost) return;\n \t\t\tsetIsStacked(ghost.scrollHeight > LINE_HEIGHT_PX);\n-\t\t}, [value]);\n+\t\t}, [value, composerWidth]);\n+\n+\t\t// Both measurements above are keyed on the draft, so a width change without an\n+\t\t// edit leaves the layout stale \u2014 the draft can wrap at one width and not the\n+\t\t// other. Track the measured column's width and re-run them when it moves.\n+\t\tuseLayoutEffect(() => {\n+\t\t\tconst column = ghostColumnRef.current;\n+\t\t\tif (!column) return;\n+\t\t\tconst observer = new ResizeObserver((entries) => {\n+\t\t\t\tconst entry = entries[0];\n+\t\t\t\tif (entry) setComposerWidth(entry.contentRect.width);\n+\t\t\t});\n+\t\t\tobserver.observe(column);\n+\t\t\treturn () => observer.disconnect();\n+\t\t}, []);\n \n \t\t// Calculate autocomplete suggestion using useMemo\n \t\tconst suggestion = useMemo(() => {\n@@ -569,7 +586,7 @@ export const TextInput = forwardRef<TextInputRef, TextInputProps>(\n \t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-hidden\n \t\t\t\t\t\t\tclassName=\"pointer-events-none invisible absolute inset-x-0 top-0 flex h-0 items-start overflow-hidden\"\n \t\t\t\t\t\t>\n-\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div className=\"min-w-0 flex-1\">\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div ref={ghostColumnRef} className=\"min-w-0 flex-1\">\n \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{/* Padding-x and line-height decide where text wraps, so they\n \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t    match the textarea; padding-y is left off on purpose. */}\n \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span\n", "test_patch": "", "problem_statement": "[Bug]: Chat composer can retain stale layout after its width changes\n### Prerequisites\n\n- [x] I have searched the existing [issues](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/issues) and [discussions](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/discussions), and this is not a duplicate.\n- [x] This is a bug, not a usage question. (For questions, please use [Discussions](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/discussions/new?category=general) instead.)\n\n### Background / Description\n\nThe chat composer measures text wrapping when the draft changes. Resizing the composer without editing the draft can leave the stacked layout and textarea height out of sync with the available width.\n\nTo reproduce, enter a draft that fits on one line in a wide window. Narrow the window until the same draft wraps, then widen it again without editing the draft. The composer should update its layout and textarea height in both directions.\n\nI propose observing the composer container\u2019s width and reusing the existing wrapping and height calculations when that width changes.\n\n### Error Messages\n\n```shell\nNo error message is known. The suspected symptom is that the chat composer retains its previous layout or textarea height after its width changes.\n```\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Open a chat session in the AgentScope Web UI.\n2. In a wide browser window, type a draft that just fits on one line. Leave it unsent.\n3. Narrow the window until the same draft wraps. Do not edit the draft.\n4. Widen the window until the draft fits on one line again.\n\nExpected: The textarea height and composer layout update in both directions as the available width changes.\n\nSuspected behavior: The textarea height or composer layout stays stale until the draft is edited.\n\n### Environment\n\n- Component: AgentScope Web UI chat composer (`TextInput.tsx`)\n- Branch inspected: `main`\n- Browser and OS: Runtime reproduction has not yet been verified.\n- Evidence: Source inspection. The wrapping measurement runs when the draft changes, and the textarea height is recalculated when the draft or stacked layout changes.\n", "hints_text": "I tested this locally on the latest `main` fetched today (`048055c9`), with both the frontend and backend running from that revision, using Chrome on macOS. I couldn't reproduce the reported stale composer layout when narrowing and widening the window without editing the draft.\n\nCould you share a concrete draft text, the window/viewport sizes that trigger the issue, and ideally a screen recording? That would help verify the behavior.\n", "created_at": "2026-11-11T08:55:37Z"}
{"repo": "agentscope-ai/agentscope", "pull_number": 3947, "instance_id": "agentscope-ai__agentscope-3947", "issue_numbers": ["3946"], "base_commit": "02cf7666c9421facab8c725df7cbe3445c76f4ac", "patch": "diff --git a/src/agentscope/formatter/_gemini_formatter.py b/src/agentscope/formatter/_gemini_formatter.py\nindex 7aaac8d6ad..f1d05bd92f 100644\n--- a/src/agentscope/formatter/_gemini_formatter.py\n+++ b/src/agentscope/formatter/_gemini_formatter.py\n@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@\n     DataBlock,\n     ToolCallBlock,\n     ToolResultBlock,\n+    ToolResultState,\n     URLSource,\n     Base64Source,\n )\n@@ -279,13 +280,20 @@ async def format(\n                         multimodal_data,\n                     ) = self.convert_tool_result_to_string(block.output)\n \n+                    # Gemini reads a failed call from the \"error\" key of the\n+                    # response, and a successful one from \"output\".\n+                    response_key = (\n+                        \"error\"\n+                        if block.state == ToolResultState.ERROR\n+                        else \"output\"\n+                    )\n                     tool_result_parts.append(\n                         {\n                             \"function_response\": {\n                                 \"id\": block.id,\n                                 \"name\": block.name,\n                                 \"response\": {\n-                                    \"output\": textual_output,\n+                                    response_key: textual_output,\n                                 },\n                             },\n                         },\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/tests/formatter_gemini_test.py b/tests/formatter_gemini_test.py\nindex b2a9b05a68..3169bc1062 100644\n--- a/tests/formatter_gemini_test.py\n+++ b/tests/formatter_gemini_test.py\n@@ -1232,6 +1232,89 @@ async def test_tool_call_with_incomplete_input_does_not_crash(\n         ][0][\"function_call\"]\n         self.assertIsInstance(function_call[\"args\"], dict)\n \n+    async def test_chat_formatter_failed_tool_result_uses_error_key(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"A failed tool call reaches Gemini under the ``error`` key of the\n+        function response, a successful one under ``output``.\"\"\"\n+        res = await GeminiChatFormatter().format(\n+            [\n+                AssistantMsg(\n+                    name=\"assistant\",\n+                    content=[\n+                        ToolCallBlock(\n+                            id=\"call_1\",\n+                            name=\"get_weather\",\n+                            input='{\"city\": \"Paris\"}',\n+                        ),\n+                        ToolCallBlock(\n+                            id=\"call_2\",\n+                            name=\"get_weather\",\n+                            input='{\"city\": \"Atlantis\"}',\n+                        ),\n+                        ToolResultBlock(\n+                            id=\"call_1\",\n+                            name=\"get_weather\",\n+                            output=[TextBlock(text=\"sunny\")],\n+                            state=ToolResultState.SUCCESS,\n+                        ),\n+                        ToolResultBlock(\n+                            id=\"call_2\",\n+                            name=\"get_weather\",\n+                            output=[TextBlock(text=\"Unknown city: Atlantis\")],\n+                            state=ToolResultState.ERROR,\n+                        ),\n+                    ],\n+                ),\n+            ],\n+        )\n+\n+        self.assertListEqual(\n+            res,\n+            [\n+                {\n+                    \"role\": \"model\",\n+                    \"parts\": [\n+                        {\n+                            \"function_call\": {\n+                                \"id\": \"call_1\",\n+                                \"name\": \"get_weather\",\n+                                \"args\": {\"city\": \"Paris\"},\n+                            },\n+                        },\n+                        {\n+                            \"function_call\": {\n+                                \"id\": \"call_2\",\n+                                \"name\": \"get_weather\",\n+                                \"args\": {\"city\": \"Atlantis\"},\n+                            },\n+                        },\n+                    ],\n+                },\n+                {\n+                    \"role\": \"user\",\n+                    \"parts\": [\n+                        {\n+                            \"function_response\": {\n+                                \"id\": \"call_1\",\n+                                \"name\": \"get_weather\",\n+                                \"response\": {\"output\": \"sunny\"},\n+                            },\n+                        },\n+                        {\n+                            \"function_response\": {\n+                                \"id\": \"call_2\",\n+                                \"name\": \"get_weather\",\n+                                \"response\": {\n+                                    \"error\": \"Unknown city: Atlantis\",\n+                                },\n+                            },\n+                        },\n+                    ],\n+                },\n+            ],\n+        )\n+\n \n class GeminiMultiAgentSystemMessageTest(IsolatedAsyncioTestCase):\n     \"\"\"A system message must never emit a ``text: None`` part.\"\"\"\n", "problem_statement": "[Bug]: Gemini formatter sends failed tool results under \"output\" instead of \"error\"\n### Description\n\n`GeminiChatFormatter` serializes every tool result as `function_response.response = {\"output\": <text>}`, whatever `ToolResultBlock.state` is. A failed tool execution (`ToolResultState.ERROR`) therefore reaches Gemini in the same shape as a successful one. `GeminiMultiAgentFormatter` delegates tool sequences to the chat formatter, so it is affected too.\n\nThe google-genai `FunctionResponse.response` field is documented as using the `\"output\"` key for the function output and the `\"error\"` key for error details, and the SDK's own `FunctionResponse.from_mcp_response` uses `{\"error\": ...}` for an MCP result with `isError` set.\n\nThis is the Gemini counterpart of #3901 (fixed for the Anthropic formatter in #3905). Existing issues and PRs were searched; no other report covers the Gemini formatter.\n\n### Reproduce (offline, no credentials)\n\n```python\nimport asyncio\nfrom agentscope.formatter import GeminiChatFormatter\nfrom agentscope.message import AssistantMsg, ToolCallBlock, ToolResultBlock, ToolResultState\n\nmsgs = [AssistantMsg(name=\"a\", content=[\n    ToolCallBlock(id=\"c1\", name=\"get_weather\", input='{\"city\": \"Atlantis\"}'),\n    ToolResultBlock(id=\"c1\", name=\"get_weather\", output=\"Unknown city\", state=ToolResultState.ERROR),\n])]\nprint(asyncio.run(GeminiChatFormatter().format(msgs))[-1])\n# main: ... 'function_response': {..., 'response': {'output': 'Unknown city'}}\n```\n\n### Expected\n\nAn `ERROR` result is sent as `{\"error\": <text>}`; other states keep `{\"output\": <text>}`, as #3905 maps only `ERROR` for Anthropic. The error text is already visible to the model today, so this restores the structured error signal rather than fixing a crash.\n\nA fix is ready and will be linked here.\n\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-11-11T05:55:50Z"}
{"repo": "agentscope-ai/agentscope", "pull_number": 3907, "instance_id": "agentscope-ai__agentscope-3907", "issue_numbers": ["3904"], "base_commit": "d74b833943d84ba8e6b8440b0fd4d46bcdc59569", "patch": "diff --git a/src/agentscope/model/_openai_chat/_model.py b/src/agentscope/model/_openai_chat/_model.py\nindex f6d12b3301..111462425a 100644\n--- a/src/agentscope/model/_openai_chat/_model.py\n+++ b/src/agentscope/model/_openai_chat/_model.py\n@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@\n \"\"\"The OpenAI Chat Completions model implementation.\"\"\"\n import base64\n from collections import OrderedDict\n+from collections.abc import Mapping\n from datetime import datetime\n from typing import Literal, Any, AsyncGenerator, TYPE_CHECKING, List, Type\n \n@@ -284,9 +285,14 @@ async def _call_api(\n         response = await self.client.chat.completions.create(**kwargs)\n \n         audio_cfg = kwargs.get(\"audio\")\n+        extra_body = kwargs.get(\"extra_body\")\n+        if isinstance(extra_body, Mapping):\n+            # The SDK merges extra_body over the request at the top level.\n+            # Decode the format actually sent, including per-call overrides.\n+            audio_cfg = extra_body.get(\"audio\", audio_cfg)\n         audio_fmt = (\n             audio_cfg.get(\"format\", \"wav\")\n-            if isinstance(audio_cfg, dict)\n+            if isinstance(audio_cfg, Mapping)\n             else \"wav\"\n         )\n \n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/tests/model_openai_chat_test.py b/tests/model_openai_chat_test.py\nindex 9aeb8453d2..045e98b70a 100644\n--- a/tests/model_openai_chat_test.py\n+++ b/tests/model_openai_chat_test.py\n@@ -8,14 +8,19 @@\n   1 final ChatResponse (is_last=True) with the full accumulated content.\n \"\"\"\n import base64\n+import copy\n import io\n+import json\n import struct\n import wave\n+from functools import partial\n from typing import Any\n import unittest\n from unittest import IsolatedAsyncioTestCase\n from unittest.mock import AsyncMock, MagicMock\n \n+import httpx\n+\n from utils import AnyString\n \n from agentscope.message import (\n@@ -37,6 +42,22 @@\n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n \n \n+def _wav() -> bytes:\n+    \"\"\"Return a valid silent WAV instead of a header-shaped byte fixture.\"\"\"\n+    output = io.BytesIO()\n+    with wave.open(output, \"wb\") as audio:\n+        audio.setnchannels(1)\n+        audio.setsampwidth(2)\n+        audio.setframerate(24000)\n+        audio.writeframes(b\"\\x00\\x00\" * 24)\n+    return output.getvalue()\n+\n+\n+def _audio(format_name: str) -> dict:\n+    \"\"\"Build a complete audio request accepted by the provider.\"\"\"\n+    return {\"voice\": \"alloy\", \"format\": format_name}\n+\n+\n def _make_model(stream: bool = False) -> Any:\n     return OpenAIChatModel(\n         credential=OpenAICredential(api_key=\"test\"),\n@@ -489,6 +510,126 @@ async def test_thinking_response(\n         )\n \n \n+class TestOpenAIChatAudioFormat(IsolatedAsyncioTestCase):\n+    \"\"\"The parser and transport agree on the effective non-stream format.\"\"\"\n+\n+    async def test_effective_audio_format_and_override_precedence(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Instance and per-call extra_body overrides follow SDK precedence.\"\"\"\n+        cases = [\n+            (\"default_pcm\", None, {}, \"pcm16\"),\n+            (\"direct_wav\", None, {\"audio\": _audio(\"wav\")}, \"wav\"),\n+            (\"instance_wav\", {\"audio\": _audio(\"wav\")}, {}, \"wav\"),\n+            (\"instance_mp3\", {\"audio\": _audio(\"mp3\")}, {}, \"mp3\"),\n+            (\n+                \"extra_beats_direct\",\n+                {\"audio\": _audio(\"wav\")},\n+                {\"audio\": _audio(\"pcm16\")},\n+                \"wav\",\n+            ),\n+            (\n+                \"per_call_extra\",\n+                {\"audio\": _audio(\"mp3\")},\n+                {\"extra_body\": {\"audio\": _audio(\"wav\")}},\n+                \"wav\",\n+            ),\n+            (\n+                \"unrelated_extra\",\n+                {\"offline_option\": True},\n+                {\"audio\": _audio(\"wav\")},\n+                \"wav\",\n+            ),\n+        ]\n+        original_wav = _wav()\n+        for name, extra_body, generate_kwargs, expected_format in cases:\n+            with self.subTest(case=name):\n+                before = copy.deepcopy((extra_body, generate_kwargs))\n+                captured = []\n+\n+                def handle(\n+                    request: httpx.Request,\n+                    recorded: list,\n+                ) -> httpx.Response:\n+                    data = json.loads(request.content)\n+                    recorded.append(data)\n+                    wire_format = data[\"audio\"][\"format\"]\n+                    payload = {\n+                        \"wav\": original_wav,\n+                        \"pcm16\": b\"\\x00\\x00\" * 24,\n+                        \"mp3\": b\"ID3-offline-fixture\",\n+                    }[wire_format]\n+                    return httpx.Response(\n+                        200,\n+                        json={\n+                            \"id\": \"chatcmpl-offline\",\n+                            \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n+                            \"created\": 1,\n+                            \"model\": \"gpt-audio\",\n+                            \"choices\": [\n+                                {\n+                                    \"index\": 0,\n+                                    \"message\": {\n+                                        \"role\": \"assistant\",\n+                                        \"content\": None,\n+                                        \"audio\": {\n+                                            \"id\": \"audio_1\",\n+                                            \"data\": base64.b64encode(\n+                                                payload,\n+                                            ).decode(),\n+                                            \"transcript\": \"hello\",\n+                                            \"expires_at\": 9999999999,\n+                                        },\n+                                    },\n+                                    \"finish_reason\": \"stop\",\n+                                },\n+                            ],\n+                            \"usage\": {\n+                                \"prompt_tokens\": 1,\n+                                \"completion_tokens\": 1,\n+                                \"total_tokens\": 2,\n+                            },\n+                        },\n+                    )\n+\n+                async with httpx.AsyncClient(\n+                    transport=httpx.MockTransport(\n+                        partial(handle, recorded=captured),\n+                    ),\n+                ) as client:\n+                    model = OpenAIChatModel(\n+                        credential=OpenAICredential(api_key=\"offline-test\"),\n+                        model=\"gpt-audio\",\n+                        stream=False,\n+                        parameters=OpenAIChatModel.Parameters(voice=\"alloy\"),\n+                        extra_body=extra_body,\n+                        client_kwargs={\"http_client\": client},\n+                    )\n+                    response = await model([], **generate_kwargs)\n+                self.assertEqual(\n+                    captured[0][\"audio\"][\"format\"],\n+                    expected_format,\n+                )\n+                source = next(\n+                    block.source\n+                    for block in response.content\n+                    if block.type == \"data\"\n+                )\n+                payload = base64.b64decode(source.data)\n+                if expected_format == \"mp3\":\n+                    self.assertEqual(source.media_type, \"audio/mp3\")\n+                    self.assertEqual(payload, b\"ID3-offline-fixture\")\n+                else:\n+                    self.assertEqual(source.media_type, \"audio/wav\")\n+                    self.assertEqual(payload, original_wav)\n+                    with wave.open(io.BytesIO(payload), \"rb\") as audio:\n+                        self.assertEqual(\n+                            audio.readframes(24),\n+                            b\"\\x00\\x00\" * 24,\n+                        )\n+                self.assertEqual((extra_body, generate_kwargs), before)\n+\n+\n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n # Streaming tests\n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n", "problem_statement": "[Bug]: OpenAIChatModel corrupts non-streaming WAV output when extra_body overrides audio.format\n### Prerequisites\n\n- [x] Searched existing issues, PRs and discussions; related reports and the remaining difference are described below.\n- [x] This is a reproducible defect report, not a usage question.\n\n### Background / Description\n\nWith parameters.voice set, OpenAIChatModel defaults to requesting PCM16 audio and wraps it in a WAV container. An SDK extra_body override specifying audio.format=wav changes the actual outgoing JSON to request an already-encoded WAV, while the parser still uses the earlier local PCM16 format.\n\nIt therefore adds a second WAV header and interprets the original RIFF header as audio samples. Passing the identical audio object directly as a per-call audio kwarg produces the same request but preserves the correct WAV bytes.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\nSave the example as `repro.py` and run `python repro.py`.\n\nAgentScope main d26173c9d1d8476a77fd673525ed71b7cc0f8f9b (2.0.12.dev0), Python 3.12.14, Windows; openai 3.48.0, httpx2 2.16.0. Run this offline example. It uses the public API, real SDK and external MockTransport; no live provider call or real API key is needed.\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Offline real SDK proof: extra_body audio.format is ignored by decoder.\"\"\"\nimport asyncio\nimport base64\nimport io\nimport json\nimport wave\nimport httpx2\nfrom agentscope.model import OpenAIChatModel\nfrom agentscope.credential import OpenAICredential\nfrom agentscope.message import UserMsg\n\n\nasync def main():\n    sound = io.BytesIO()\n    with wave.open(sound, \"wb\") as wav:\n        wav.setnchannels(1)\n        wav.setsampwidth(2)\n        wav.setframerate(24000)\n        wav.writeframes(b\"\\x00\\x00\" * 24)\n    original = sound.getvalue()\n    results = {}\n    for via_extra in (False, True):\n        wire = []\n        def handle(request):\n            wire.append(json.loads(request.content))\n            return httpx2.Response(200, json={\"id\":\"chatcmpl-offline\", \"object\":\"chat.completion\", \"created\":1,\"model\":\"gpt-audio\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":None,\"audio\":{\"id\":\"audio_1\",\"data\":base64.b64encode(original).decode(),\"transcript\":\"hello\",\"expires_at\":9999999999}},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":1,\"completion_tokens\":1,\"total_tokens\":2}})\n        async with httpx2.AsyncClient(transport=httpx2.MockTransport(handle)) as client:\n            model = OpenAIChatModel(credential=OpenAICredential(api_key=\"offline-dummy\",base_url=\"http://offline.test\"),model=\"gpt-audio\",parameters=OpenAIChatModel.Parameters(voice=\"alloy\"),stream=False,extra_body={\"audio\":{\"voice\":\"alloy\",\"format\":\"wav\"}} if via_extra else None,client_kwargs={\"http_client\":client})\n            output = await model([UserMsg(name=\"user\",content=\"Speak\")], **({} if via_extra else {\"audio\":{\"voice\":\"alloy\",\"format\":\"wav\"}}))\n        block = next(b for b in output.content if b.type == \"data\")\n        payload = base64.b64decode(block.source.data)\n        with wave.open(io.BytesIO(payload), \"rb\") as wav:\n            frame_prefix = wav.readframes(2).hex()\n        results[\"extra_body\" if via_extra else \"direct_audio_kwarg\"] = {\"wire_audio\":wire[0][\"audio\"],\"media_type\":block.source.media_type,\"same_bytes\":payload==original,\"input_bytes\":len(original),\"output_bytes\":len(payload),\"sample_prefix\":frame_prefix}\n    print(json.dumps(results))\n    assert results[\"extra_body\"][\"same_bytes\"], \"Already-encoded WAV was wrapped as raw PCM, corrupting audio\"\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    asyncio.run(main())\n```\n\n### Actual / Expected\n\nThe Python wave-generated fixture is a valid 92-byte silent mono 24 kHz PCM16 WAV. Both cases send audio.format=wav through the real OpenAI SDK.\n\n- Direct audio kwarg: 92-byte identical output, initial decoded samples 00000000.\n- extra_body override: 136-byte output, initial decoded samples 52494646 (RIFF), still labelled audio/wav.\n\nThe byte-equality assertion fails. Expected: resolve the effective wire format before decoding; do not wrap an already-encoded WAV as raw PCM.\n\n### Related reports / scope\n\nSearched open/closed issues and PRs for audio/WAV and extra_body audio. Merged PR #3028 adds the correct wrapper for actual PCM16 output; this report concerns SDK extra_body overriding the format used by that parser. Streamed size fix #3242 is separate. A focused fix should cover normal PCM wrapping, direct overrides and extra_body overrides.\n\nPrepared with Codex assistance. Executed locally against unchanged upstream source. Full upstream tests, lint, types, build and live inference were not run; no implementation or human-review completion is claimed.\n\n\n", "hints_text": "/assign me\nThis issue is still being verified. Please comment again once it is confirmed, and it is yours.\n/assign me\nIt's yours, @wang1299. If there is no pull request and no word from you by 2026-11-24 the claim is released so nobody is blocked \u2014 a comment here renews it.", "created_at": "2026-11-10T03:21:41Z"}
{"repo": "agentscope-ai/agentscope", "pull_number": 3906, "instance_id": "agentscope-ai__agentscope-3906", "issue_numbers": ["3902"], "base_commit": "d74b833943d84ba8e6b8440b0fd4d46bcdc59569", "patch": "diff --git a/src/agentscope/model/_ollama/_model.py b/src/agentscope/model/_ollama/_model.py\nindex 4cd2413e5f..5752ae44ab 100644\n--- a/src/agentscope/model/_ollama/_model.py\n+++ b/src/agentscope/model/_ollama/_model.py\n@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@\n # -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n \"\"\"The Ollama chat model implementation.\"\"\"\n+import inspect\n import json\n from datetime import datetime\n from typing import Literal, Any, AsyncGenerator, TYPE_CHECKING, List, Type\n@@ -256,49 +257,60 @@ async def _parse_stream_response(\n         text_id: str = _generate_id()\n         thinking_id: str = _generate_id()\n \n-        async for chunk in response:\n-            delta_res = ChatResponse(\n-                content=[],\n-                is_last=False,\n-                id=response_id,\n-            )\n-\n-            msg = chunk.message\n-\n-            # Thinking\n-            if getattr(msg, \"thinking\", None):\n-                delta_res.append_thinking(\n-                    block_id=thinking_id,\n-                    thinking=msg.thinking,\n+        try:\n+            async for chunk in response:\n+                delta_res = ChatResponse(\n+                    content=[],\n+                    is_last=False,\n+                    id=response_id,\n                 )\n \n-            # Text\n-            if msg.content:\n-                delta_res.append_text(\n-                    block_id=text_id,\n-                    text=msg.content,\n-                )\n-\n-            # Tool call. The ollama client drops the server's call id, and\n-            # one built from the position repeats in the next round\n-            for tool_call in msg.tool_calls or []:\n-                delta_res.append_tool_call(\n-                    block_id=_generate_id(),\n-                    name=tool_call.function.name,\n-                    input=json.dumps(\n-                        tool_call.function.arguments,\n-                        ensure_ascii=False,\n-                    ),\n+                msg = chunk.message\n+\n+                # Thinking\n+                if getattr(msg, \"thinking\", None):\n+                    delta_res.append_thinking(\n+                        block_id=thinking_id,\n+                        thinking=msg.thinking,\n+                    )\n+\n+                # Text\n+                if msg.content:\n+                    delta_res.append_text(\n+                        block_id=text_id,\n+                        text=msg.content,\n+                    )\n+\n+                # The client drops the server's call id; positions repeat\n+                # in the next round, so allocate a fresh id per call.\n+                for tool_call in msg.tool_calls or []:\n+                    delta_res.append_tool_call(\n+                        block_id=_generate_id(),\n+                        name=tool_call.function.name,\n+                        input=json.dumps(\n+                            tool_call.function.arguments,\n+                            ensure_ascii=False,\n+                        ),\n+                    )\n+\n+                current_time = (\n+                    datetime.now() - start_datetime\n+                ).total_seconds()\n+                delta_res.usage = ChatUsage(\n+                    input_tokens=getattr(chunk, \"prompt_eval_count\", 0) or 0,\n+                    output_tokens=getattr(chunk, \"eval_count\", 0) or 0,\n+                    time=current_time,\n                 )\n \n-            current_time = (datetime.now() - start_datetime).total_seconds()\n-            delta_res.usage = ChatUsage(\n-                input_tokens=getattr(chunk, \"prompt_eval_count\", 0) or 0,\n-                output_tokens=getattr(chunk, \"eval_count\", 0) or 0,\n-                time=current_time,\n-            )\n-\n-            yield delta_res\n+                yield delta_res\n+        finally:\n+            # Closing the parser does not implicitly close its delegated\n+            # SDK generator. Await its response cleanup before returning.\n+            aclose = getattr(response, \"aclose\", None)\n+            if aclose is not None:\n+                result = aclose()\n+                if inspect.isawaitable(result):\n+                    await result\n \n     async def _parse_completion_response(\n         self,\n", "test_patch": "", "problem_statement": "[Bug]: OllamaChatModel does not close the SDK HTTP stream on awaited early aclose\n### Prerequisites\n\n- [x] Searched existing issues, PRs and discussions; related reports and the remaining difference are described below.\n- [x] This is a reproducible defect report, not a usage question.\n\n### Background / Description\n\nClosing the stream returned by public OllamaChatModel after its first delta returns while the underlying Ollama SDK HTTP response body is still open. Fully consuming the same response closes the body.\n\nThis report concerns the native Ollama adapter's inner delegation. It does not use Agent.reply_stream(). The base model wrapper already awaits closure of its delegated parser, but the Ollama parser uses a bare async-for over the SDK stream without closing it when that parser exits early.\n\nThis delays releasing the provider response until later finalization. No permanent connection leak or billing impact has been measured.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\nSave the example as `repro.py` and run `python repro.py`.\n\nAgentScope main d26173c9d1d8476a77fd673525ed71b7cc0f8f9b (2.0.12.dev0), Python 3.12.14, Windows; ollama 0.6.3, httpx 0.28.1. Run this offline example. It uses the public API, real SDK and external MockTransport; no live provider call or real API key is needed.\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Offline public OllamaChatModel + real Ollama SDK + HTTPX transport.\"\"\"\nimport asyncio\nimport gc\nimport json\n\nimport httpx\nfrom agentscope.model import OllamaChatModel\nfrom agentscope.credential import OllamaCredential\nfrom agentscope.message import UserMsg\n\n\nclass Body(httpx.AsyncByteStream):\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.closed = False\n\n    async def __aiter__(self):\n        yield b'{\"model\":\"test\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"hello\"},\"done\":false}\\n'\n        yield b'{\"model\":\"test\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\" world\"},\"done\":false}\\n'\n        yield b'{\"model\":\"test\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"\"},\"done\":true,\"prompt_eval_count\":1,\"eval_count\":2}\\n'\n\n    async def aclose(self):\n        self.closed = True\n\n\nasync def case(early):\n    body = Body()\n    model = OllamaChatModel(\n        model=\"test\", credential=OllamaCredential(host=\"http://offline.test\"),\n        client_kwargs={\"transport\": httpx.MockTransport(lambda request: httpx.Response(200, stream=body))},\n    )\n    stream = await model([UserMsg(name=\"user\", content=\"hello\")])\n    if early:\n        await anext(stream)\n        await stream.aclose()\n    else:\n        async for _ in stream:\n            pass\n    # Don't depend on eventual garbage collection to release a network stream.\n    result = {\"early\": early, \"closed_before_gc\": body.closed}\n    gc.collect()\n    await asyncio.sleep(0)\n    result[\"closed_after_gc_one_turn\"] = body.closed\n    return result\n\n\nasync def main():\n    complete = await case(False)\n    early = await case(True)\n    print(json.dumps({\"complete\": complete, \"early_close\": early}))\n    assert early[\"closed_before_gc\"], \"await model_stream.aclose() returned with HTTP stream still open\"\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    asyncio.run(main())\n```\n\n### Actual / Expected\n\nFull consumption: closed_before_gc is true. After the first delta and awaited stream.aclose(): closed_before_gc is false, remaining false after GC and one event-loop turn. The assertion fails.\n\nExpected: the owned provider body is closed before the awaited public aclose returns.\n\n### Related reports / scope\n\nRelated #3210 fixes the base-wrapper-to-parser boundary, already present on this main. #3683 / PR #3707 fix Agent reasoning delegation and use the OpenAI-compatible adapter. This direct native Ollama reproduction still fails despite the base cleanup. A focused fix should close the owned SDK iterator in the Ollama parser, with actual transport and asynchronous-cleanup regressions.\n\nPrepared with Codex assistance. Executed locally against unchanged upstream source. Full upstream tests, lint, types, build and live inference were not run; no implementation or human-review completion is claimed.\n\n\n", "hints_text": "/assign me\nThis issue is still being verified. Please comment again once it is confirmed, and it is yours.\n/assign me\nIt's yours, @wang1299. If there is no pull request and no word from you by 2026-11-24 the claim is released so nobody is blocked \u2014 a comment here renews it.", "created_at": "2026-11-10T03:15:29Z"}
{"repo": "agentscope-ai/agentscope", "pull_number": 3905, "instance_id": "agentscope-ai__agentscope-3905", "issue_numbers": ["3901"], "base_commit": "d74b833943d84ba8e6b8440b0fd4d46bcdc59569", "patch": "diff --git a/src/agentscope/formatter/_anthropic_formatter.py b/src/agentscope/formatter/_anthropic_formatter.py\nindex fd2790716b..9e483989bd 100644\n--- a/src/agentscope/formatter/_anthropic_formatter.py\n+++ b/src/agentscope/formatter/_anthropic_formatter.py\n@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@\n     DataBlock,\n     ToolCallBlock,\n     ToolResultBlock,\n+    ToolResultState,\n     URLSource,\n     Base64Source,\n )\n@@ -244,13 +245,14 @@ async def _format_messages(\n                             {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"(empty tool output)\"},\n                         )\n \n-                    content_blocks.append(\n-                        {\n-                            \"type\": \"tool_result\",\n-                            \"tool_use_id\": block.id,\n-                            \"content\": tool_result_content,\n-                        },\n-                    )\n+                    tool_result: dict[str, Any] = {\n+                        \"type\": \"tool_result\",\n+                        \"tool_use_id\": block.id,\n+                        \"content\": tool_result_content,\n+                    }\n+                    if block.state == ToolResultState.ERROR:\n+                        tool_result[\"is_error\"] = True\n+                    content_blocks.append(tool_result)\n                     # Anthropic requires tool_result to be in a \"user\" message.\n                     has_tool_result = True\n \n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/tests/formatter_anthropic_test.py b/tests/formatter_anthropic_test.py\nindex ac2e5b7ac3..d50cd29264 100644\n--- a/tests/formatter_anthropic_test.py\n+++ b/tests/formatter_anthropic_test.py\n@@ -564,6 +564,70 @@ async def test_chat_formatter_tool_result_role_forced_to_user(\n         ]\n         self.assertListEqual(tool_result_roles, [\"user\"])\n \n+    async def test_tool_result_error_state(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Only ERROR gains a flag, including when the output is empty.\"\"\"\n+        for formatter_type in (\n+            AnthropicChatFormatter,\n+            AnthropicMultiAgentFormatter,\n+        ):\n+            for state in ToolResultState:\n+                for output in (\"failed\", \"\"):\n+                    with self.subTest(\n+                        formatter=formatter_type.__name__,\n+                        state=state,\n+                        output=output,\n+                    ):\n+                        msgs = [\n+                            AssistantMsg(\n+                                name=\"assistant\",\n+                                content=[\n+                                    ToolCallBlock(\n+                                        id=\"call_1\",\n+                                        name=\"validate\",\n+                                        input=\"{}\",\n+                                    ),\n+                                    ToolResultBlock(\n+                                        id=\"call_1\",\n+                                        name=\"validate\",\n+                                        output=output,\n+                                        state=state,\n+                                    ),\n+                                ],\n+                            ),\n+                        ]\n+                        expected_result = {\n+                            \"type\": \"tool_result\",\n+                            \"tool_use_id\": \"call_1\",\n+                            \"content\": [\n+                                {\n+                                    \"type\": \"text\",\n+                                    \"text\": output or \"(empty tool output)\",\n+                                },\n+                            ],\n+                        }\n+                        if state == ToolResultState.ERROR:\n+                            expected_result[\"is_error\"] = True\n+                        self.assertEqual(\n+                            await formatter_type().format(msgs),\n+                            [\n+                                {\n+                                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n+                                    \"content\": [\n+                                        {\n+                                            \"type\": \"tool_use\",\n+                                            \"id\": \"call_1\",\n+                                            \"name\": \"validate\",\n+                                            \"input\": {},\n+                                        },\n+                                    ],\n+                                },\n+                                {\n+                                    \"role\": \"user\",\n+                                    \"content\": [expected_result],\n+                                },\n+                            ],\n+                        )\n+\n     async def test_chat_formatter_tool_result_with_image(self) -> None:\n         \"\"\"Tool result containing an image DataBlock inlines the image in the\n         tool_result content without crashing on TextBlock system-reminders.\"\"\"\ndiff --git a/tests/model_anthropic_test.py b/tests/model_anthropic_test.py\nindex 82c5063445..30f34db0a1 100644\n--- a/tests/model_anthropic_test.py\n+++ b/tests/model_anthropic_test.py\n@@ -24,6 +24,8 @@\n     AssistantMsg,\n     TextBlock,\n     ToolCallBlock,\n+    ToolResultBlock,\n+    ToolResultState,\n     ThinkingBlock,\n )\n from agentscope.model import AnthropicChatModel, ChatUsage\n@@ -272,6 +274,77 @@ async def test_tool_call_response(self) -> None:\n             ),\n         )\n \n+    async def test_tool_result_error_flag_on_wire(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"The SDK sends the error flag only for failed tool results.\"\"\"\n+        captured = []\n+        backend = (\n+            httpx2\n+            if issubclass(DefaultAsyncHttpxClient, httpx2.AsyncClient)\n+            else httpx\n+        )\n+\n+        def handle(request: Any) -> Any:\n+            captured.append(json.loads(request.content))\n+            return backend.Response(\n+                200,\n+                json={\n+                    \"id\": \"msg_1\",\n+                    \"type\": \"message\",\n+                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n+                    \"model\": \"offline\",\n+                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"ok\"}],\n+                    \"stop_reason\": \"end_turn\",\n+                    \"usage\": {\"input_tokens\": 1, \"output_tokens\": 1},\n+                },\n+            )\n+\n+        async with DefaultAsyncHttpxClient(\n+            transport=backend.MockTransport(handle),\n+        ) as client:\n+            model = AnthropicChatModel(\n+                credential=AnthropicCredential(api_key=\"offline-test\"),\n+                model=\"offline\",\n+                stream=False,\n+                client_kwargs={\"http_client\": client},\n+            )\n+            for state in (ToolResultState.ERROR, ToolResultState.SUCCESS):\n+                await model(\n+                    [\n+                        AssistantMsg(\n+                            name=\"assistant\",\n+                            content=[\n+                                ToolCallBlock(\n+                                    id=\"call_1\",\n+                                    name=\"validate\",\n+                                    input=\"{}\",\n+                                ),\n+                                ToolResultBlock(\n+                                    id=\"call_1\",\n+                                    name=\"validate\",\n+                                    output=\"failed\",\n+                                    state=state,\n+                                ),\n+                            ],\n+                        ),\n+                    ],\n+                )\n+\n+        expected_result = {\n+            \"type\": \"tool_result\",\n+            \"tool_use_id\": \"call_1\",\n+            \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"failed\"}],\n+        }\n+        self.assertEqual(\n+            [body[\"messages\"][-1] for body in captured],\n+            [\n+                {\n+                    \"role\": \"user\",\n+                    \"content\": [{**expected_result, \"is_error\": True}],\n+                },\n+                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [expected_result]},\n+            ],\n+        )\n+\n     async def test_thinking_response(self) -> None:\n         \"\"\"Non-stream response with reasoning creates ThinkingBlock.\"\"\"\n         mock_create = AsyncMock(\n", "problem_statement": "[Bug]: Anthropic formatter drops failed tool-result state instead of sending is_error\n### Prerequisites\n\n- [x] Searched existing issues, PRs and discussions; related reports and the remaining difference are described below.\n- [x] This is a reproducible defect report, not a usage question.\n\n### Background / Description\n\n`AnthropicChatFormatter` drops `ToolResultBlock.state`: an explicitly failed tool execution (`ToolResultState.ERROR`) is serialized exactly like a successful result. The outgoing `tool_result` has no `is_error` flag.\n\nAgent already preserves `ToolResponse.state` when saving tool results in its context. Losing it at the formatter boundary prevents the Claude API from distinguishing success from failure through its structured tool-result status. The error text remains present; this report does **not** claim an API rejection or that every model answer becomes incorrect.\n\nAnthropic documents `is_error: true` for tool execution errors: [Handle tool calls](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/handle-tool-calls#handling-errors-with-is_error).\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\nSave the example as `repro.py` and run `python repro.py`.\n\nOn main `d26173c9d1d8476a77fd673525ed71b7cc0f8f9b`, run this offline example (no credentials or provider call):\n\n```python\nimport asyncio\nfrom agentscope.formatter import AnthropicChatFormatter\nfrom agentscope.message import (\n    AssistantMsg, UserMsg, ToolCallBlock,\n    ToolResultBlock, ToolResultState,\n)\n\nasync def main():\n    results = {}\n    for state in (ToolResultState.SUCCESS, ToolResultState.ERROR):\n        messages = [\n            UserMsg(name=\"user\", content=\"Run validation.\"),\n            AssistantMsg(name=\"assistant\", content=[\n                ToolCallBlock(id=\"call_1\", name=\"validate\", input=\"{}\")\n            ]),\n            AssistantMsg(name=\"tool\", content=[\n                ToolResultBlock(\n                    id=\"call_1\", name=\"validate\",\n                    output=\"Validation failed: invalid input\",\n                    state=state,\n                )\n            ]),\n        ]\n        formatted = await AnthropicChatFormatter().format(messages)\n        results[state.value] = formatted[-1][\"content\"][0]\n    print(results)\n    assert results[\"error\"].get(\"is_error\") is True\n\nasyncio.run(main())\n```\n\n### Actual / Expected\n\nActual: both states produce:\n```json\n{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_1\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Validation failed: invalid input\"}]}\n```\nThe assertion fails.\n\nExpected: the ERROR result includes `\"is_error\": true`; successful results remain non-error.\n\nI also reproduced this through the public `AnthropicChatModel(stream=False)`, the real Anthropic SDK and an external in-process HTTP MockTransport: the request JSON still omits the flag. No live model request was made.\n\n### Environment\n\n- AgentScope: `2.0.12.dev0`, main SHA above\n- Python 3.12.14, Windows\n- Anthropic SDK 2.7.0 (for the additional request-boundary check)\n\n### Scope / prior search\n\nSearched open and closed issues/PRs for `is_error`, Anthropic errors, and `tool_result`. Related reports about parallel results, empty output and unsupported media concern content/turn formatting rather than the lost execution state.\n\nA focused change could map ERROR to the provider flag and cover both successful/failed results, including the inherited multi-agent formatter. No broader retry or error-policy change is proposed.\n\nPrepared with Codex assistance; the reproduction was executed locally against unchanged upstream source.\n\n", "hints_text": "/assign me\nThis issue is still being verified. Please comment again once it is confirmed, and it is yours.\n/assign me\nIt's yours, @wang1299. If there is no pull request and no word from you by 2026-11-24 the claim is released so nobody is blocked \u2014 a comment here renews it.", "created_at": "2026-11-10T03:11:03Z"}
{"repo": "agentscope-ai/agentscope", "pull_number": 3892, "instance_id": "agentscope-ai__agentscope-3892", "issue_numbers": ["3891"], "base_commit": "d8ebf89b6ce3ce904992dc0f3be0fc1be1b1211d", "patch": "diff --git a/src/agentscope/formatter/_xai_formatter.py b/src/agentscope/formatter/_xai_formatter.py\nindex 9e158cec5c..20721743bf 100644\n--- a/src/agentscope/formatter/_xai_formatter.py\n+++ b/src/agentscope/formatter/_xai_formatter.py\n@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@\n ``chat_pb2.Message`` proto objects rather than plain dicts, because the\n ``xai_sdk`` chat API accepts proto messages directly.\n \"\"\"\n+\n import base64\n from fnmatch import fnmatch\n from typing import Any, List\n@@ -158,6 +159,46 @@ async def format(\n \n         xai_messages: List[Any] = []\n \n+        def flush_assistant(\n+            text_blocks: list[TextBlock],\n+            tool_calls: list[ToolCallBlock],\n+            media: list[DataBlock],\n+        ) -> None:\n+            \"\"\"Emit one assistant segment before its tool results or hint.\"\"\"\n+            text = \"\\n\".join(block.text for block in text_blocks)\n+            media_args = _xai_user_args_from_blocks(\n+                media,\n+                image,\n+                self.supported_input_media_types,\n+            )\n+            if media_args:\n+                if text:\n+                    xai_messages.append(assistant(text))\n+                    text = \"\"\n+                # Keep promoted media ahead of the tool call/result sequence.\n+                xai_messages.append(user(*media_args))\n+\n+            if tool_calls:\n+                msg_proto = chat_pb2.Message()\n+                msg_proto.role = chat_pb2.MessageRole.Value(\"ROLE_ASSISTANT\")\n+                if text:\n+                    msg_proto.content.add().text = text\n+                for call in tool_calls:\n+                    proto_call = msg_proto.tool_calls.add()\n+                    proto_call.id = call.id\n+                    proto_call.type = chat_pb2.ToolCallType.Value(\n+                        \"TOOL_CALL_TYPE_CLIENT_SIDE_TOOL\",\n+                    )\n+                    proto_call.function.name = call.name\n+                    proto_call.function.arguments = call.input\n+                xai_messages.append(msg_proto)\n+            elif text:\n+                xai_messages.append(assistant(text))\n+\n+            text_blocks.clear()\n+            tool_calls.clear()\n+            media.clear()\n+\n         for msg in msgs:\n             blocks = msg.get_content_blocks()\n \n@@ -210,6 +251,7 @@ async def format(\n                 pending_text: list[TextBlock] = []\n                 pending_tool_calls: list[ToolCallBlock] = []\n                 pending_media: list[Any] = []\n+                assistant_media: list[DataBlock] = []\n \n                 for block in blocks:\n                     if pending_media and not isinstance(\n@@ -220,34 +262,11 @@ async def format(\n                         pending_media = []\n \n                     if isinstance(block, ToolResultBlock):\n-                        # Convert each ToolResultBlock to a tool_result\n-                        # message.\n-                        if pending_tool_calls:\n-                            msg_proto = chat_pb2.Message()\n-                            msg_proto.role = chat_pb2.MessageRole.Value(\n-                                \"ROLE_ASSISTANT\",\n-                            )\n-                            if pending_text:\n-                                c = msg_proto.content.add()\n-                                c.text = \"\\n\".join(\n-                                    b.text for b in pending_text\n-                                )\n-                                pending_text = []\n-                            for tc in pending_tool_calls:\n-                                proto_tc = msg_proto.tool_calls.add()\n-                                proto_tc.id = tc.id\n-                                proto_tc.type = chat_pb2.ToolCallType.Value(\n-                                    \"TOOL_CALL_TYPE_CLIENT_SIDE_TOOL\",\n-                                )\n-                                proto_tc.function.name = tc.name\n-                                proto_tc.function.arguments = tc.input\n-                            xai_messages.append(msg_proto)\n-                            pending_tool_calls = []\n-                        elif pending_text:\n-                            text = \"\\n\".join(b.text for b in pending_text)\n-                            if text:\n-                                xai_messages.append(assistant(text))\n-                            pending_text = []\n+                        flush_assistant(\n+                            pending_text,\n+                            pending_tool_calls,\n+                            assistant_media,\n+                        )\n \n                         (\n                             textual_output,\n@@ -262,12 +281,7 @@ async def format(\n                             ),\n                         )\n \n-                        # Promote media that came back inside the tool\n-                        # result into a following user message, which is what\n-                        # the other formatters do via the same shared helper.\n-                        # ``xai_sdk`` re-hydrates binary tool results and\n-                        # ``input_types`` already advertises images, so the\n-                        # textual hint alone would lose the picture.\n+                        # Keep tool results together before emitting media.\n                         if multimodal_data:\n                             promo_args = _xai_user_args_from_blocks(\n                                 multimodal_data,\n@@ -286,36 +300,16 @@ async def format(\n                     elif isinstance(block, ThinkingBlock):\n                         pass\n \n+                    elif isinstance(block, DataBlock):\n+                        # xAI requires media in user messages.\n+                        assistant_media.append(block)\n+\n                     elif isinstance(block, HintBlock):\n-                        if pending_tool_calls or pending_text:\n-                            if pending_tool_calls:\n-                                msg_proto = chat_pb2.Message()\n-                                msg_proto.role = chat_pb2.MessageRole.Value(\n-                                    \"ROLE_ASSISTANT\",\n-                                )\n-                                if pending_text:\n-                                    c = msg_proto.content.add()\n-                                    c.text = \"\\n\".join(\n-                                        b.text for b in pending_text\n-                                    )\n-                                    pending_text = []\n-                                for tc in pending_tool_calls:\n-                                    proto_tc = msg_proto.tool_calls.add()\n-                                    proto_tc.id = tc.id\n-                                    proto_tc.type = (\n-                                        chat_pb2.ToolCallType.Value(\n-                                            \"TOOL_CALL_TYPE_CLIENT_SIDE_TOOL\",\n-                                        )\n-                                    )\n-                                    proto_tc.function.name = tc.name\n-                                    proto_tc.function.arguments = tc.input\n-                                xai_messages.append(msg_proto)\n-                                pending_tool_calls = []\n-                            elif pending_text:\n-                                text = \"\\n\".join(b.text for b in pending_text)\n-                                if text:\n-                                    xai_messages.append(assistant(text))\n-                                pending_text = []\n+                        flush_assistant(\n+                            pending_text,\n+                            pending_tool_calls,\n+                            assistant_media,\n+                        )\n                         if isinstance(block.hint, str):\n                             xai_messages.append(user(block.hint))\n                         else:\n@@ -328,31 +322,11 @@ async def format(\n                                 xai_messages.append(user(*hint_args))\n \n                 xai_messages.extend(pending_media)\n-\n-                if pending_tool_calls:\n-                    # Assistant turn that triggered tool calls (history).\n-                    msg_proto = chat_pb2.Message()\n-                    msg_proto.role = chat_pb2.MessageRole.Value(\n-                        \"ROLE_ASSISTANT\",\n-                    )\n-                    if pending_text:\n-                        c = msg_proto.content.add()\n-                        c.text = \"\\n\".join(b.text for b in pending_text)\n-                        pending_text = []\n-                    for tc in pending_tool_calls:\n-                        proto_tc = msg_proto.tool_calls.add()\n-                        proto_tc.id = tc.id\n-                        proto_tc.type = chat_pb2.ToolCallType.Value(\n-                            \"TOOL_CALL_TYPE_CLIENT_SIDE_TOOL\",\n-                        )\n-                        proto_tc.function.name = tc.name\n-                        proto_tc.function.arguments = tc.input\n-                    xai_messages.append(msg_proto)\n-                elif pending_text:\n-                    # Regular assistant text message.\n-                    text = \"\\n\".join(b.text for b in pending_text)\n-                    if text:\n-                        xai_messages.append(assistant(text))\n+                flush_assistant(\n+                    pending_text,\n+                    pending_tool_calls,\n+                    assistant_media,\n+                )\n \n             else:\n                 logger.warning(\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/tests/formatter_xai_test.py b/tests/formatter_xai_test.py\nindex 027c81ff53..d45dd31cc6 100644\n--- a/tests/formatter_xai_test.py\n+++ b/tests/formatter_xai_test.py\n@@ -290,6 +290,43 @@ async def test_chat_formatter_image_detail_extra_param(self) -> None:\n             res,\n         )\n \n+    async def test_chat_formatter_assistant_media(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Assistant images follow their text and precede the next user.\"\"\"\n+        picture = DataBlock(\n+            source=Base64Source(\n+                data=\"SU1HX0RBVEE=\",\n+                media_type=\"image/png\",\n+            ),\n+            detail=\"high\",\n+        )\n+        for text in (\"Here is the chart.\", \"\"):\n+            with self.subTest(text=text):\n+                content = (\n+                    [TextBlock(text=text), picture] if text else [picture]\n+                )\n+                res = await XAIChatFormatter().format(\n+                    [\n+                        UserMsg(name=\"user\", content=\"Draw a chart.\"),\n+                        AssistantMsg(name=\"assistant\", content=content),\n+                        UserMsg(name=\"user\", content=\"Explain the chart.\"),\n+                    ],\n+                )\n+                expected = [user(\"Draw a chart.\")]\n+                if text:\n+                    expected.append(assistant(text))\n+                expected.extend(\n+                    [\n+                        user(\n+                            image(\n+                                \"data:image/png;base64,SU1HX0RBVEE=\",\n+                                detail=\"high\",\n+                            ),\n+                        ),\n+                        user(\"Explain the chart.\"),\n+                    ],\n+                )\n+                self.assertListEqual(expected, res)\n+\n     async def test_chat_formatter_system_message(self) -> None:\n         \"\"\"System message becomes a system() stub.\"\"\"\n         fmt = XAIChatFormatter()\n@@ -519,7 +556,7 @@ async def test_chat_formatter_tool_result_unsupported_media(\n     async def test_chat_formatter_parallel_tool_media_after_tool_msgs(\n         self,\n     ) -> None:\n-        \"\"\"Promoted media does not split parallel tool-result messages.\"\"\"\n+        \"\"\"Assistant media precedes tools; result media follows all results.\"\"\"\n         fmt = XAIChatFormatter()\n         picture = DataBlock(\n             id=\"image_1\",\n@@ -533,6 +570,13 @@ async def test_chat_formatter_parallel_tool_media_after_tool_msgs(\n                 AssistantMsg(\n                     name=\"assistant\",\n                     content=[\n+                        TextBlock(text=\"Original chart.\"),\n+                        DataBlock(\n+                            source=URLSource(\n+                                url=\"https://example.com/original.png\",\n+                                media_type=\"image/png\",\n+                            ),\n+                        ),\n                         ToolCallBlock(\n                             id=\"call_shot\",\n                             name=\"screenshot\",\n@@ -558,6 +602,7 @@ async def test_chat_formatter_parallel_tool_media_after_tool_msgs(\n                             output=[TextBlock(text=\"Example Domain\")],\n                             state=ToolResultState.SUCCESS,\n                         ),\n+                        TextBlock(text=\"New chart analysis.\"),\n                     ],\n                 ),\n             ],\n@@ -565,8 +610,8 @@ async def test_chat_formatter_parallel_tool_media_after_tool_msgs(\n \n         normalized_res = [\n             (\n-                res[0].role,\n-                [part.text for part in res[0].content],\n+                msg.role,\n+                [part.text for part in msg.content],\n                 [\n                     (\n                         tool_call.id,\n@@ -574,14 +619,18 @@ async def test_chat_formatter_parallel_tool_media_after_tool_msgs(\n                         tool_call.function.name,\n                         tool_call.function.arguments,\n                     )\n-                    for tool_call in res[0].tool_calls\n+                    for tool_call in msg.tool_calls\n                 ],\n-            ),\n-            *res[1:],\n+            )\n+            if hasattr(msg, \"tool_calls\")\n+            else msg\n+            for msg in res\n         ]\n         self.assertListEqual(\n             normalized_res,\n             [\n+                assistant(\"Original chart.\"),\n+                user(image(\"https://example.com/original.png\")),\n                 (\n                     2,\n                     [],\n@@ -618,6 +667,65 @@ async def test_chat_formatter_parallel_tool_media_after_tool_msgs(\n                     image(\"https://example.com/shot.png\"),\n                     \"</system-reminder>\",\n                 ),\n+                assistant(\"New chart analysis.\"),\n+            ],\n+        )\n+\n+    async def test_chat_formatter_media_before_separate_tool_result(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Media must not separate a tool call from a later result message.\"\"\"\n+        res = await XAIChatFormatter().format(\n+            [\n+                AssistantMsg(\n+                    name=\"assistant\",\n+                    content=[\n+                        DataBlock(\n+                            source=URLSource(\n+                                url=\"https://example.com/original.png\",\n+                                media_type=\"image/png\",\n+                            ),\n+                        ),\n+                        ToolCallBlock(id=\"call_1\", name=\"edit\", input=\"{}\"),\n+                    ],\n+                ),\n+                AssistantMsg(\n+                    name=\"assistant\",\n+                    content=[\n+                        ToolResultBlock(\n+                            id=\"call_1\",\n+                            name=\"edit\",\n+                            output=\"Done.\",\n+                            state=ToolResultState.SUCCESS,\n+                        ),\n+                    ],\n+                ),\n+            ],\n+        )\n+        normalized_res = [\n+            (\n+                msg.role,\n+                [part.text for part in msg.content],\n+                [\n+                    (\n+                        call.id,\n+                        call.type,\n+                        call.function.name,\n+                        call.function.arguments,\n+                    )\n+                    for call in msg.tool_calls\n+                ],\n+            )\n+            if hasattr(msg, \"tool_calls\")\n+            else msg\n+            for msg in res\n+        ]\n+        self.assertListEqual(\n+            normalized_res,\n+            [\n+                user(image(\"https://example.com/original.png\")),\n+                (2, [], [(\"call_1\", 1, \"edit\", \"{}\")]),\n+                tool_result(\"Done.\", tool_call_id=\"call_1\"),\n             ],\n         )\n \n@@ -1030,6 +1138,52 @@ async def test_chat_formatter_hint_block(self) -> None:\n             res,\n         )\n \n+    async def test_chat_formatter_assistant_media_around_hint(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Assistant images stay with their segment on either side of hints.\"\"\"\n+        before = DataBlock(\n+            source=URLSource(\n+                url=\"https://example.com/before.png\",\n+                media_type=\"image/png\",\n+            ),\n+        )\n+        after = DataBlock(\n+            source=URLSource(\n+                url=\"https://example.com/after.png\",\n+                media_type=\"image/png\",\n+            ),\n+        )\n+        for hint in (\n+            \"Revise the chart.\",\n+            [TextBlock(text=\"Revise the chart.\")],\n+        ):\n+            for text in (\"Original chart.\", \"\"):\n+                with self.subTest(hint=hint, text=text):\n+                    content = [TextBlock(text=text)] if text else []\n+                    res = await XAIChatFormatter().format(\n+                        [\n+                            AssistantMsg(\n+                                name=\"assistant\",\n+                                content=[\n+                                    *content,\n+                                    before,\n+                                    HintBlock(hint=hint),\n+                                    TextBlock(text=\"Revised chart.\"),\n+                                    after,\n+                                ],\n+                            ),\n+                        ],\n+                    )\n+                    expected = [assistant(text)] if text else []\n+                    expected.extend(\n+                        [\n+                            user(image(\"https://example.com/before.png\")),\n+                            user(\"Revise the chart.\"),\n+                            assistant(\"Revised chart.\"),\n+                            user(image(\"https://example.com/after.png\")),\n+                        ],\n+                    )\n+                    self.assertListEqual(expected, res)\n+\n     async def test_chat_formatter_hint_block_multimodal(self) -> None:\n         \"\"\"Multimodal HintBlock becomes one user() stub carrying text +\n         image.\"\"\"\n", "problem_statement": "XAIChatFormatter drops images carried by assistant messages\n## Problem\n\n`XAIChatFormatter.format` handles a different set of block types for the `user` role than for the `assistant` role, and the assistant branch has no `DataBlock` case at all \u2014 nor a fallback `else`:\n\n```python\nelif isinstance(block, ToolCallBlock):\n    pending_tool_calls.append(block)\nelif isinstance(block, TextBlock):\n    pending_text.append(block)\nelif isinstance(block, ThinkingBlock):\n    pass\nelif isinstance(block, HintBlock):\n    ...\n```\n\nThe user branch right above it handles `DataBlock` and warns on anything unrecognised:\n\n```python\nelif isinstance(block, DataBlock):\n    content_args.extend(_xai_user_args_from_blocks(...))\nelse:\n    logger.warning(\"Unsupported block type %s in user message, skipped.\", ...)\n```\n\nSo any image or other `DataBlock` carried by an assistant message is discarded without a payload entry and without a log line.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nWith an assistant message that has both text and an image:\n\n```\nA) image on a USER message (control)\n   payload : [user('look', _StubImage(url='data:image/png;base64,SU1HX0RBVEE='))]\n   image forwarded: True\n\nB) image on an ASSISTANT message\n   payload : [user('draw a chart'), assistant('Here is the chart')]\n   image forwarded: False\n```\n\nAn assistant message that is *only* an image disappears completely \u2014 the turn vanishes from the payload:\n\n```\nC) assistant message that is ONLY an image\n   messages in : 2\n   payload     : [user('draw a chart')]\n```\n\n## Why this is reachable\n\n`XAIChatFormatter` is the default formatter of `XAIChatModel`, so every xAI request goes through it. Assistant-authored media is not exotic: a team or multi-agent setup relays a member's reply as a `ToolResultBlock` whose output preserves `DataBlock`s, and a coordinator that re-observes inter-agent history can place assistant messages with images into an xAI agent's context.\n\nThe other providers forward the identical message \u2014 OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, DashScope, Volcengine, Moonshot, the OpenAI-Response formatter and Ollama all keep the image \u2014 so xAI is the outlier.\n\nThe existing `tests/formatter_xai_test.py` (28 tests, all passing) exercises images only in user messages, in `ToolResultBlock.output`, and in `HintBlock.hint`. No test puts a `DataBlock` directly on an assistant `Msg`, so nothing pins the current lossy behaviour.\n\n## Fix\n\nCollect assistant-authored media and promote it into a user message *after* the assistant turn has been emitted:\n\n```python\nelif isinstance(block, DataBlock):\n    assistant_media.append(block)\n...\n# after the assistant turn is appended\nif assistant_media:\n    promo_args = _xai_user_args_from_blocks(\n        assistant_media,\n        image,\n        self.supported_input_media_types,\n    )\n    if promo_args:\n        xai_messages.append(user(*promo_args))\n```\n\nPlacing it after rather than before matters: appending during the block loop puts the promoted user message ahead of the assistant text, which reorders the conversation. Promoting after the turn keeps `user \u2192 assistant \u2192 media \u2192 next user` in the original order.\n\nThis reuses the same `_xai_user_args_from_blocks` helper and `supported_input_media_types` check the user branch already uses, so an unsupported media type follows the established behaviour.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/formatter_xai_assistant_media_test.py`:\n\n- `test_assistant_media_is_promoted_after_its_turn` \u2014 the image reaches the payload and lands after the assistant turn (fails on `main`)\n- `test_image_only_assistant_message_is_not_lost` \u2014 the turn survives and the payload has two entries (fails on `main`)\n- `test_user_media_is_still_forwarded_inline` \u2014 the user path is unchanged\n\nAll 28 existing formatter tests still pass alongside these. Happy to send it as a PR.\n\n", "hints_text": "Thanks for the report, @lianbie. To keep the tracker focused, each account can have at most 5 open issues at a time, so this one is closed for now. Once your open issues are resolved, feel free to reopen it.", "created_at": "2026-11-09T09:54:53Z"}
{"repo": "agentscope-ai/agentscope", "pull_number": 3889, "instance_id": "agentscope-ai__agentscope-3889", "issue_numbers": ["3890", "3884"], "base_commit": "d286c31e4d6d13bfbb065385ad31b901ae10f8c3", "patch": "diff --git a/src/agentscope/mcp/_mcp_client.py b/src/agentscope/mcp/_mcp_client.py\nindex 849c5304c8..f57a0f7433 100644\n--- a/src/agentscope/mcp/_mcp_client.py\n+++ b/src/agentscope/mcp/_mcp_client.py\n@@ -137,6 +137,11 @@ class MCPClient(BaseModel):\n     _close_requested: asyncio.Event | None = PrivateAttr(default=None)\n     _is_connected: bool = PrivateAttr(default=False)\n     _cached_tools: list[mcp.types.Tool] | None = PrivateAttr(default=None)\n+    _tool_list_generation: int = PrivateAttr(default=0)\n+    _discovery_task: asyncio.Task[list[mcp.types.Tool]] | None = PrivateAttr(\n+        default=None,\n+    )\n+    _discovery_waiters: int = PrivateAttr(default=0)\n     _http_client: httpx2.AsyncClient | None = PrivateAttr(default=None)\n     _static_headers: httpx2.Headers | None = PrivateAttr(default=None)\n     _runtime_headers: dict[str, str] = PrivateAttr(default_factory=dict)\n@@ -239,6 +244,7 @@ async def _handle_server_message(self, message: Any) -> None:\n         from a connection that no longer matches them.\n         \"\"\"\n         if isinstance(message, mcp.types.ToolListChangedNotification):\n+            self._tool_list_generation += 1\n             self._cached_tools = None\n \n     def _create_http_client(\n@@ -498,20 +504,10 @@ async def list_raw_tools(self) -> list[mcp.types.Tool]:\n                 Raw MCP tool descriptors after filtering.\n \n         Raises:\n-            RuntimeError: If not connected (for stateful connections).\n+            RuntimeError: If not connected (for stateful connections), or\n+                if tool-list notifications invalidate both discovery attempts.\n         \"\"\"\n-        if not self.is_stateful:\n-            # Stateless: create a temporary auto-negotiating client.\n-            async with self._get_client_gen() as client:\n-                res = await client.list_tools(cache_mode=\"refresh\")\n-                self._cached_tools = res.tools\n-        else:\n-            # Stateful: use the existing high-level client.\n-            self._validate_connection()\n-            res = await self._client.list_tools(cache_mode=\"refresh\")\n-            self._cached_tools = res.tools\n-\n-        available_tools: list = self._cached_tools\n+        available_tools = await self._discover_tools()\n         if self.enable_tools is not None:\n             available_tools = [\n                 tool\n@@ -524,6 +520,51 @@ async def list_raw_tools(self) -> list[mcp.types.Tool]:\n             ]\n         return available_tools\n \n+    async def _discover_tools(self) -> list[mcp.types.Tool]:\n+        \"\"\"Share stateless discovery without sharing caller cancellation.\"\"\"\n+        if self.is_stateful:\n+            return await self._fetch_tools()\n+\n+        task = self._discovery_task\n+        if task is None or task.done():\n+            task = asyncio.create_task(self._fetch_tools())\n+            self._discovery_task = task\n+            self._discovery_waiters = 0\n+        self._discovery_waiters += 1\n+        try:\n+            return await asyncio.shield(task)\n+        finally:\n+            if self._discovery_task is task:\n+                self._discovery_waiters -= 1\n+                if self._discovery_waiters == 0:\n+                    self._discovery_task = None\n+                    if not task.done():\n+                        # No callers remain to use the temporary connection.\n+                        task.cancel()\n+                        await asyncio.gather(task, return_exceptions=True)\n+                    elif not task.cancelled():\n+                        task.exception()\n+\n+    async def _fetch_tools(self) -> list[mcp.types.Tool]:\n+        \"\"\"Fetch and cache a catalog that survives the invalidation fence.\"\"\"\n+        # Retry once if a notification invalidates the in-flight tool list.\n+        for _ in range(2):\n+            if not self.is_stateful:\n+                async with self._get_client_gen() as client:\n+                    generation = self._tool_list_generation\n+                    res = await client.list_tools(cache_mode=\"refresh\")\n+            else:\n+                self._validate_connection()\n+                generation = self._tool_list_generation\n+                res = await self._client.list_tools(cache_mode=\"refresh\")\n+            if generation == self._tool_list_generation:\n+                self._cached_tools = res.tools\n+                return res.tools\n+        raise RuntimeError(\n+            f\"MCP {self.name!r} tool list changed during discovery; \"\n+            \"retry the lookup.\",\n+        )\n+\n     async def list_tools(self) -> list[ToolBase]:\n         \"\"\"List available tools from the MCP server as wrapped\n         :class:`ToolBase` instances. If `enable_tools` and `disable_tools`\n@@ -565,10 +606,11 @@ async def get_tool(\n         # Avoid circular import by importing here\n         from ..tool import MCPTool\n \n-        if self._cached_tools is None:\n-            await self.list_raw_tools()\n+        tools = self._cached_tools\n+        if tools is None:\n+            tools = await self._discover_tools()\n         target_tool = next(\n-            (tool for tool in self._cached_tools or [] if tool.name == name),\n+            (tool for tool in tools if tool.name == name),\n             None,\n         )\n         if target_tool is None:\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/tests/mcp_client_list_changed_test.py b/tests/mcp_client_list_changed_test.py\nindex 0f68478d77..02ee03c604 100644\n--- a/tests/mcp_client_list_changed_test.py\n+++ b/tests/mcp_client_list_changed_test.py\n@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@\n # -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n \"\"\"Tests for tool-cache invalidation on tools/list_changed notifications.\"\"\"\n # pylint: disable=protected-access\n+import asyncio\n from types import TracebackType\n from typing import Any\n from unittest.async_case import IsolatedAsyncioTestCase\n@@ -8,7 +9,7 @@\n \n import mcp.types\n \n-from agentscope.mcp import MCPClient, StdioMCPConfig\n+from agentscope.mcp import HttpMCPConfig, MCPClient, StdioMCPConfig\n \n \n class _FakeTransport:\n@@ -144,3 +145,357 @@ async def test_unrelated_notifications_keep_cached_tools(self) -> None:\n             (\"mcp__list_changed__echo\", 1),\n         )\n         self.assertIs(client._cached_tools, cached)\n+\n+\n+class MCPClientConcurrentDiscoveryTest(IsolatedAsyncioTestCase):\n+    \"\"\"Coordinate concurrent discovery and connection cleanup with events.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def setUp(self) -> None:\n+        self.started = asyncio.Event()\n+        self.release = asyncio.Event()\n+        self.connections: list[_FakeClient] = []\n+        self.closed: list[_FakeClient] = []\n+        self.closing = asyncio.Event()\n+        self.close_gate: asyncio.Event | None = None\n+        self.notify_on_enter = True\n+        self.error: Exception | None = None\n+        self.catalog = [\n+            mcp.types.Tool(name=name, inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\"})\n+            for name in (\"echo\", \"hidden\")\n+        ]\n+        case = self\n+\n+        class ControlledClient(_FakeClient):\n+            \"\"\"Hold a snapshot until the test releases its response.\"\"\"\n+\n+            async def __aenter__(self) -> \"ControlledClient\":\n+                case.connections.append(self)\n+                if case.notify_on_enter:\n+                    await self.message_handler(\n+                        mcp.types.ToolListChangedNotification(\n+                            method=\"notifications/tools/list_changed\",\n+                        ),\n+                    )\n+                return self\n+\n+            async def list_tools(\n+                self,\n+                **_kwargs: Any,\n+            ) -> mcp.types.ListToolsResult:\n+                snapshot = mcp.types.ListToolsResult(tools=case.catalog)\n+                case.started.set()\n+                await case.release.wait()\n+                if case.error is not None:\n+                    raise case.error\n+                return snapshot\n+\n+            async def __aexit__(self, *args: Any) -> bool:\n+                if case.close_gate is not None:\n+                    case.closing.set()\n+                    await case.close_gate.wait()\n+                case.closed.append(self)\n+                return False\n+\n+        self.enterContext(\n+            patch(\"agentscope.mcp._mcp_client.SDKClient\", ControlledClient),\n+        )\n+        self.client = MCPClient(\n+            name=\"concurrent\",\n+            is_stateful=False,\n+            mcp_config=HttpMCPConfig(url=\"http://mcp.invalid/mcp\"),\n+        )\n+\n+    async def _start(\n+        self,\n+        entry: str = \"list\",\n+        name: str = \"echo\",\n+    ) -> asyncio.Task[Any]:\n+        \"\"\"Wait until the caller has joined discovery before returning.\"\"\"\n+        joined = asyncio.Event()\n+\n+        async def lookup() -> Any:\n+            joined.set()\n+            if entry == \"get\":\n+                return await self.client.get_tool(name)\n+            return await self.client.list_raw_tools()\n+\n+        task = asyncio.create_task(lookup())\n+        self.addAsyncCleanup(self._cancel, task)\n+        await joined.wait()\n+        return task\n+\n+    async def _cancel(self, task: asyncio.Task[Any]) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Drain caller tasks even when an assertion fails.\"\"\"\n+        if self.close_gate is not None:\n+            self.close_gate.set()\n+        task.cancel()\n+        await asyncio.gather(task, return_exceptions=True)\n+\n+    async def test_concurrent_discovery_shares_one_connection(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Connection notifications must not multiply discovery attempts.\"\"\"\n+        for notify in (False, True):\n+            for callers in (2, 8):\n+                with self.subTest(notify=notify, callers=callers):\n+                    self.notify_on_enter = notify\n+                    self.started.clear()\n+                    self.release.clear()\n+                    self.connections.clear()\n+                    self.closed.clear()\n+                    tasks = [await self._start() for _ in range(callers)]\n+                    await self.started.wait()\n+                    self.release.set()\n+                    results = await asyncio.gather(*tasks)\n+                    self.assertEqual(results, [self.catalog] * callers)\n+                    self.assertEqual(len(self.connections), 1)\n+                    self.assertEqual(self.closed, self.connections)\n+                    self.assertIsNone(self.client._discovery_task)\n+\n+    async def test_get_and_list_share_unfiltered_discovery(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Filtering must not hide tools from concurrent direct lookups.\"\"\"\n+        self.client.enable_tools = [\"echo\"]\n+        listed = await self._start()\n+        hidden = await self._start(\"get\", \"hidden\")\n+        await self.started.wait()\n+        self.release.set()\n+        raw, tool = await asyncio.gather(listed, hidden)\n+        self.assertEqual(raw, self.catalog[:1])\n+        self.assertEqual(tool.name, \"mcp__concurrent__hidden\")\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client._cached_tools, self.catalog)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(self.connections), 1)\n+\n+    async def test_connection_notifications_do_not_cause_ping_pong(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Sibling connection notifications must not exhaust both attempts.\"\"\"\n+        entered = [asyncio.Event() for _ in range(4)]\n+        case = self\n+\n+        class PingPongClient(_FakeClient):\n+            \"\"\"Release each old response after the next connection opens.\"\"\"\n+\n+            index: int = 0\n+\n+            async def __aenter__(self) -> \"PingPongClient\":\n+                self.index = len(case.connections)\n+                case.connections.append(self)\n+                if self.index:\n+                    await self.message_handler(\n+                        mcp.types.ToolListChangedNotification(\n+                            method=\"notifications/tools/list_changed\",\n+                        ),\n+                    )\n+                entered[self.index].set()\n+                return self\n+\n+            async def list_tools(\n+                self,\n+                **_kwargs: Any,\n+            ) -> mcp.types.ListToolsResult:\n+                if self.index == 0:\n+                    await case.release.wait()\n+                elif self.index < 3:\n+                    await entered[self.index + 1].wait()\n+                return mcp.types.ListToolsResult(tools=case.catalog)\n+\n+        with patch(\"agentscope.mcp._mcp_client.SDKClient\", PingPongClient):\n+            first = await self._start()\n+            await entered[0].wait()\n+            second = await self._start()\n+            self.release.set()\n+            results = await asyncio.wait_for(\n+                asyncio.gather(first, second, return_exceptions=True),\n+                timeout=5,\n+            )\n+        self.assertEqual(results, [self.catalog, self.catalog])\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client._cached_tools, self.catalog)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(self.connections), 1)\n+\n+    async def test_other_session_notification_fences_shared_cache(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"A notification outside discovery must still reject its snapshot.\"\"\"\n+        callers = [await self._start() for _ in range(2)]\n+        await self.started.wait()\n+        self.catalog = [\n+            mcp.types.Tool(name=\"new\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\"}),\n+        ]\n+        async with self.client._get_client_gen():\n+            self.release.set()\n+            results = await asyncio.gather(*callers)\n+        self.assertEqual(results, [self.catalog, self.catalog])\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client._cached_tools, self.catalog)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(self.connections), 3)\n+\n+    async def test_cancelled_caller_does_not_cancel_other_waiters(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Either the first caller or a follower may cancel independently.\"\"\"\n+        for cancelled in (0, 1):\n+            with self.subTest(cancelled=cancelled):\n+                self.started.clear()\n+                self.release.clear()\n+                self.connections.clear()\n+                self.closed.clear()\n+                callers = [await self._start() for _ in range(2)]\n+                await self.started.wait()\n+                await self._cancel(callers[cancelled])\n+                self.assertEqual(self.closed, [])\n+                self.release.set()\n+                result = await callers[1 - cancelled]\n+                self.assertEqual(result, self.catalog)\n+                self.assertEqual(self.closed, self.connections)\n+                self.assertEqual(len(self.connections), 1)\n+                self.assertIsNone(self.client._discovery_task)\n+\n+    async def test_last_cancelled_caller_closes_connection(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Abandoned discovery must close and allow a subsequent request.\"\"\"\n+        callers = [await self._start() for _ in range(2)]\n+        await self.started.wait()\n+        for caller in callers:\n+            await self._cancel(caller)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.closed, self.connections)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(self.connections), 1)\n+        self.assertIsNone(self.client._discovery_task)\n+        self.assertIsNone(self.client._cached_tools)\n+        self.release.set()\n+        self.assertEqual(await self.client.list_raw_tools(), self.catalog)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(self.connections), 2)\n+\n+    async def test_failed_discovery_reaches_all_callers_and_can_retry(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"A failed shared task must not poison later discovery.\"\"\"\n+        self.error = RuntimeError(\"discovery failed\")\n+        callers = [await self._start() for _ in range(2)]\n+        await self.started.wait()\n+        self.release.set()\n+        results = await asyncio.gather(*callers, return_exceptions=True)\n+        self.assertEqual(results, [self.error, self.error])\n+        self.assertEqual(self.closed, self.connections)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(self.connections), 1)\n+        self.assertIsNone(self.client._discovery_task)\n+        self.error = None\n+        self.assertEqual(await self.client.list_raw_tools(), self.catalog)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(self.connections), 2)\n+\n+    async def test_cancelled_cleanup_does_not_clear_new_discovery(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"A fresh caller may arrive while the abandoned connection closes.\"\"\"\n+        self.close_gate = asyncio.Event()\n+        first = await self._start()\n+        await self.started.wait()\n+        first.cancel()\n+        await self.closing.wait()\n+        self.started.clear()\n+        second = await self._start()\n+        await self.started.wait()\n+        active = self.client._discovery_task\n+        self.close_gate.set()\n+        await asyncio.gather(first, return_exceptions=True)\n+        self.assertIs(self.client._discovery_task, active)\n+        self.assertFalse(second.done())\n+        self.release.set()\n+        self.assertEqual(await second, self.catalog)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.closed, self.connections)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(self.connections), 2)\n+        self.assertIsNone(self.client._discovery_task)\n+\n+\n+class MCPClientListGenerationTest(IsolatedAsyncioTestCase):\n+    \"\"\"Reject tool lists invalidated during discovery.\"\"\"\n+\n+    async def test_discovery_crossing_notification_uses_new_catalog(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Retry stale responses once in both connection modes.\"\"\"\n+        for stateful in (False, True):\n+            for entry in (\"list\", \"get\"):\n+                for repeated in (False, True):\n+                    with self.subTest(\n+                        stateful=stateful,\n+                        entry=entry,\n+                        repeated=repeated,\n+                    ):\n+                        await self._check(stateful, entry, repeated)\n+\n+    async def _check(\n+        self,\n+        stateful: bool,\n+        entry: str,\n+        repeated: bool,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        calls = 0\n+\n+        class RacingClient(_FakeClient):\n+            \"\"\"Notify after taking a tool-list snapshot.\"\"\"\n+\n+            async def __aenter__(self) -> \"RacingClient\":\n+                # Pre-request notifications must not invalidate the response.\n+                await self.message_handler(\n+                    mcp.types.ToolListChangedNotification(\n+                        method=\"notifications/tools/list_changed\",\n+                    ),\n+                )\n+                return self\n+\n+            async def list_tools(\n+                self,\n+                **_kwargs: Any,\n+            ) -> mcp.types.ListToolsResult:\n+                nonlocal calls\n+                calls += 1\n+                if calls > 3:\n+                    raise AssertionError(\"Discovery retried without a bound\")\n+                name = \"old\" if calls == 1 else \"new\"\n+                snapshot = mcp.types.ListToolsResult(\n+                    tools=[\n+                        mcp.types.Tool(\n+                            name=name,\n+                            inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\"},\n+                        ),\n+                    ],\n+                )\n+                if calls == 1 or repeated:\n+                    await self.message_handler(\n+                        mcp.types.ToolListChangedNotification(\n+                            method=\"notifications/tools/list_changed\",\n+                        ),\n+                    )\n+                return snapshot\n+\n+        with patch(\n+            \"agentscope.mcp._mcp_client.stdio_client\",\n+            return_value=_FakeTransport(),\n+        ), patch(\"agentscope.mcp._mcp_client.SDKClient\", RacingClient):\n+            client = MCPClient(\n+                name=\"generation\",\n+                is_stateful=stateful,\n+                mcp_config=StdioMCPConfig(command=\"unused\")\n+                if stateful\n+                else HttpMCPConfig(url=\"http://mcp.invalid/mcp\"),\n+            )\n+            if stateful:\n+                await client.connect()\n+            try:\n+                if repeated:\n+                    with self.assertRaisesRegex(RuntimeError, \"changed\"):\n+                        if entry == \"get\":\n+                            await client.get_tool(\"new\")\n+                        else:\n+                            await client.list_raw_tools()\n+                    self.assertIsNone(client._cached_tools)\n+                else:\n+                    if entry == \"list\":\n+                        result = await client.list_raw_tools()\n+                        self.assertEqual(\n+                            [tool.name for tool in result],\n+                            [\"new\"],\n+                        )\n+                    await client.get_tool(\"new\")\n+                    with self.assertRaises(ValueError):\n+                        await client.get_tool(\"old\")\n+                self.assertEqual(calls, 2)\n+            finally:\n+                if stateful:\n+                    await client.close()\n", "problem_statement": "test(app): fix race in background task renewal fairness test\n## AgentScope Version\n\n2.0.12dev\n\n## Description\n\nFix an intermittent failure in\n`TestRedisBackgroundTaskRecords.test_renewal_budget_preserves_fairness_and_cancels_io`, introduced in #1865 and reported on Windows: `AssertionError: 0 not greater than or equal to 2`\n\nThe renewal scheduler starts during task registration, before the stalled-I/O mock is installed. When registration overlaps a renewal round, the test can observe all task IDs before either mocked head task has been cancelled.\n\nGate renewal with an `asyncio.Event` until all six tasks are registered and the mock is installed. This makes the initial queue order deterministic while preserving the fairness, concurrency, cancellation, and shutdown assertions.\n\nThis change only affects test setup and requires no migration or\nuser-facing docume\n\n## Checklist\n\nPlease check the following items before code is ready to be reviewed.\n\n- [ ]  An issue has been created for this PR\n- [ ]  I have read the [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ]  Docstrings are in Google style\n- [ ]  Related documentation has been updated (e.g. links, examples, etc.) in [documentation repository](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/docs)\n- [ ]  Code is ready for review\n[Bug]: MCP tools/list response can repopulate an invalidated tool cache\n### Prerequisites\r\n- [x] I searched existing issues and PRs.\r\n- [x] This is a reproducible bug.\r\n\r\n### Environment\r\nAgentScope main `27c52cc65088227bb7414cb665c1bbbdef18f220`, Python 3.12, Windows. No Docker or live model credentials are required.\r\n\r\n### Background / Description\r\nA tools/list request may snapshot the old catalog, then the server sends tools/list_changed before that request returns. `_handle_server_message` clears `_cached_tools`, but `list_raw_tools` subsequently assigns the older response unconditionally. Later get_tool calls see a nonempty cache and keep using stale schemas or fail to find newly added tools.\r\n\r\nThe reproduction uses a real stdio JSON-RPC process and the installed MCP SDK. The peer waits until AgentScope has processed the notification before returning the old snapshot. This is within one connection, distinct from reconnect issue #2898; it is an interleaving missing from the ordinary notification invalidation fixed in #3733.\r\n\r\n### Observed result\r\nControl: echo_v2 is discoverable on all three lookups. Race: the notification was processed, but the first list is echo_v1 and all three subsequent get_tool(\"echo_v2\") calls fail. Explicit list_raw_tools refresh restores discovery.\r\n\r\n### Proposed fix\r\nTrack tool-list invalidation generations. Discard a response whose request crossed an invalidation and retry discovery with a bounded retry count; never re-publish that response as a valid cache. If the catalog keeps changing, report a retryable discovery error rather than loop forever. Keep stateful/stateless paths and existing enable/disable filtering. No public API changes or lock held across network I/O.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nSave the following files together and run the `probe_*.py` file with AgentScope installed from the above revision. All resources are local and cleaned up.\r\n\r\n#### mcp_list_race_peer.py\r\n```python\r\n\"\"\"JSON-RPC peer: a tools snapshot straddles a tools/list_changed event.\"\"\"\r\nimport json\r\nimport sys\r\nimport time\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nack = Path(sys.argv[1])\r\nmode = sys.argv[2]\r\nlists = 0\r\n\r\ndef send(value):\r\n    print(json.dumps(value), flush=True)\r\n\r\nfor line in sys.stdin:\r\n    request = json.loads(line)\r\n    if \"id\" not in request:\r\n        continue\r\n    method = request[\"method\"]\r\n    result = {}\r\n    if method == \"initialize\":\r\n        result = {\"protocolVersion\": request[\"params\"][\"protocolVersion\"], \"capabilities\": {\"tools\": {\"listChanged\": True}}, \"serverInfo\": {\"name\": \"list-race-peer\", \"version\": \"1\"}}\r\n    elif method == \"tools/list\":\r\n        lists += 1\r\n        name = \"echo_v2\"\r\n        if lists == 1 and mode == \"race\":\r\n            name = \"echo_v1\"  # Snapshot taken before the server updates its catalog.\r\n            send({\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"method\": \"notifications/tools/list_changed\"})\r\n            deadline = time.monotonic() + 10\r\n            while not ack.exists():\r\n                if time.monotonic() > deadline:\r\n                    raise RuntimeError(\"Client never processed list_changed\")\r\n                time.sleep(0.01)\r\n        result = {\"tools\": [{\"name\": name, \"inputSchema\": {\"type\": \"object\"}}]}\r\n    send({\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": request[\"id\"], \"result\": result})\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### probe_mcp_list_notification_race.py\r\n```python\r\n\"\"\"Real stdio MCP peer, SDK, and AgentScope cache; no production edits.\"\"\"\r\nimport asyncio\r\nimport json\r\nimport sys\r\nimport tempfile\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nimport mcp.types\r\nfrom agentscope.mcp import MCPClient, StdioMCPConfig\r\n\r\n\r\nasync def run(mode):\r\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as directory:\r\n        ack = Path(directory) / \"notification-handled\"\r\n\r\n        class ObservedClient(MCPClient):\r\n            async def _handle_server_message(self, message):\r\n                await super()._handle_server_message(message)\r\n                if isinstance(message, mcp.types.ToolListChangedNotification):\r\n                    ack.write_text(\"handled\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\r\n\r\n        client = ObservedClient(name=\"race\", is_stateful=True, mcp_config=StdioMCPConfig(command=sys.executable, args=[str(Path(__file__).with_name(\"mcp_list_race_peer.py\")), str(ack), mode]))\r\n        await client.connect()\r\n        try:\r\n            initial = await client.list_raw_tools()\r\n            failures = 0\r\n            for _ in range(3):\r\n                try:\r\n                    await client.get_tool(\"echo_v2\")\r\n                except ValueError:\r\n                    failures += 1\r\n            refreshed = await client.list_raw_tools()\r\n            await client.get_tool(\"echo_v2\")\r\n            result = {\"mode\": mode, \"notification_processed_before_response\": ack.exists(), \"first_tools\": [t.name for t in initial], \"next_three_lookups_failed\": failures, \"explicit_refresh\": [t.name for t in refreshed]}\r\n            assert failures == (3 if mode == \"race\" else 0), result\r\n            print(json.dumps(result))\r\n        finally:\r\n            await client.close()\r\n\r\n\r\nasync def main():\r\n    for mode in (\"control\", \"race\"):\r\n        await asyncio.wait_for(run(mode), 20)\r\n\r\nasyncio.run(main())\r\n\r\n```\r\n\n", "hints_text": "\n/assign me\nIt's yours, @qkycir. If there is no pull request and no word from you by 2026-11-23 the claim is released so nobody is blocked \u2014 a comment here renews it.", "created_at": "2026-11-09T09:15:25Z"}
{"repo": "agentscope-ai/agentscope", "pull_number": 3887, "instance_id": "agentscope-ai__agentscope-3887", "issue_numbers": ["3885", "3890"], "base_commit": "d286c31e4d6d13bfbb065385ad31b901ae10f8c3", "patch": "diff --git a/src/agentscope/app/middleware/_tool_offload_middleware.py b/src/agentscope/app/middleware/_tool_offload_middleware.py\nindex e5fe4deebd..012b754fcd 100644\n--- a/src/agentscope/app/middleware/_tool_offload_middleware.py\n+++ b/src/agentscope/app/middleware/_tool_offload_middleware.py\n@@ -227,7 +227,7 @@ async def on_acting(  # type:ignore[override]\n         # ----------------------------------------------------------------\n         # Wrap next_handler in a Task, draining output into a Queue\n         # ----------------------------------------------------------------\n-        queue: asyncio.Queue = asyncio.Queue()\n+        queue: asyncio.Queue | None = asyncio.Queue()\n \n         async def _drain_to_queue() -> ToolResponse | None:\n             \"\"\"Drain output and return the terminal tool outcome.\"\"\"\n@@ -236,16 +236,20 @@ async def _drain_to_queue() -> ToolResponse | None:\n                 async for item in next_handler(**input_kwargs):\n                     if isinstance(item, ToolResponse):\n                         response = item\n-                    await queue.put(item)\n+                    if queue is not None:\n+                        queue.put_nowait(item)\n+                    del item\n             except Exception as exc:  # pylint: disable=broad-except\n-                await queue.put(exc)\n+                if queue is not None:\n+                    queue.put_nowait(exc)\n                 response = ToolResponse(\n                     id=tool_call.id,\n                     state=ToolResultState.ERROR,\n                     content=[TextBlock(text=str(exc))],\n                 )\n             finally:\n-                await queue.put(_QUEUE_SENTINEL)\n+                if queue is not None:\n+                    queue.put_nowait(_QUEUE_SENTINEL)\n             return response\n \n         drain_task: asyncio.Task = asyncio.create_task(_drain_to_queue())\n@@ -292,6 +296,14 @@ async def _drain_to_queue() -> ToolResponse | None:\n             drain_task.cancel()\n             return\n \n+        # The deliverer awaits the final response directly. Drop the queue\n+        # and foreground references before yielding: nobody consumes further\n+        # stream events, and a bounded queue here would deadlock the producer.\n+        # No await separates this transition from the producer's queue check.\n+        queue = None\n+        pre_collected.clear()\n+        item = None\n+\n         # ----------------------------------------------------------------\n         # Timeout path: spawn deliverer, register drain_task, yield synthetic\n         # ----------------------------------------------------------------\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/tests/tool_offload_middleware_test.py b/tests/tool_offload_middleware_test.py\nindex 86d2452220..7bb8ce078e 100644\n--- a/tests/tool_offload_middleware_test.py\n+++ b/tests/tool_offload_middleware_test.py\n@@ -2,7 +2,9 @@\n # pylint: disable=protected-access\n \"\"\"Unit tests for ToolOffloadMiddleware.\"\"\"\n import asyncio\n+import gc\n import json\n+import weakref\n from typing import Any, AsyncGenerator\n from unittest.async_case import IsolatedAsyncioTestCase\n from unittest.mock import AsyncMock, MagicMock\n@@ -235,6 +237,101 @@ async def test_fast_tool_completes_normally(self) -> None:\n         # No background tasks registered\n         self.assertEqual(len(self.bg_manager.tasks), 0)\n \n+    async def test_offloaded_stream_releases_intermediate_chunks(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Detaching the foreground releases old and future stream events.\"\"\"\n+        for outcome in (\"success\", \"error\", \"cancel\"):\n+            with self.subTest(outcome=outcome):\n+                await self._check_stream_retention(outcome)\n+\n+    async def _check_stream_retention(self, outcome: str) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Run one isolated producer/consumer handoff.\"\"\"\n+        agent, middleware = self._make_agent(\n+            Toolkit(tools=[SlowTool()]),\n+            timeout_secs=0.01,\n+        )\n+        start = asyncio.Event()\n+        streamed = asyncio.Event()\n+        finish = asyncio.Event()\n+        delivered = asyncio.Event()\n+        refs: list[weakref.ReferenceType] = []\n+\n+        async def handler(**_kwargs: Any) -> AsyncGenerator:\n+            \"\"\"Emit a foreground chunk and a background burst.\"\"\"\n+            item = ToolChunk(content=[TextBlock(text=\"foreground\")])\n+            refs.append(weakref.ref(item))\n+            yield item\n+            del item\n+            await start.wait()\n+            for index in range(32):\n+                item = ToolChunk(\n+                    content=[\n+                        TextBlock(\n+                            text=f\"{index}:\" + \"x\" * 65536,\n+                        ),\n+                    ],\n+                )\n+                refs.append(weakref.ref(item))\n+                yield item\n+                del item\n+            streamed.set()\n+            await finish.wait()\n+            if outcome == \"error\":\n+                raise ValueError(\"stream failed\")\n+            yield ToolResponse(\n+                id=\"stream-retention\",\n+                content=[TextBlock(text=\"done\")],\n+            )\n+\n+        async def push(key: str, *_args: Any, **_kwargs: Any) -> None:\n+            \"\"\"Observe real notification delivery without sleeps.\"\"\"\n+            if key == MessageBusKeys.inbox(agent.state.session_id):\n+                delivered.set()\n+\n+        middleware._message_bus.queue_push.side_effect = push\n+        stream = middleware.on_acting(\n+            agent,\n+            {\n+                \"tool_call\": ToolCallBlock(\n+                    id=\"stream-retention\",\n+                    name=\"slow_tool\",\n+                    input=\"{}\",\n+                ),\n+            },\n+            handler,\n+        )\n+        await asyncio.wait_for(anext(stream), 2)\n+        task = next(iter(self.bg_manager.tasks.values())).asyncio_task\n+        try:\n+            # Keep on_acting suspended at its synthetic response too.\n+            start.set()\n+            await asyncio.wait_for(streamed.wait(), 2)\n+            gc.collect()\n+            self.assertEqual(sum(ref() is not None for ref in refs), 0)\n+            if outcome == \"cancel\":\n+                task.cancel()\n+                await asyncio.gather(task, return_exceptions=True)\n+                self.assertFalse(delivered.is_set())\n+            else:\n+                finish.set()\n+                await asyncio.wait_for(delivered.wait(), 2)\n+                push_calls = middleware._message_bus.queue_push.call_args_list\n+                calls = [\n+                    call\n+                    for call in push_calls\n+                    if call.args[0]\n+                    == MessageBusKeys.inbox(agent.state.session_id)\n+                ]\n+                self.assertEqual(len(calls), 1)\n+                self.assertIn(\n+                    \"stream failed\" if outcome == \"error\" else \"done\",\n+                    str(calls[0]),\n+                )\n+        finally:\n+            start.set()\n+            finish.set()\n+            await asyncio.gather(task, return_exceptions=True)\n+            await stream.aclose()\n+\n     async def test_slow_tool_offloaded_to_background(self) -> None:\n         \"\"\"A tool that exceeds timeout returns a synthetic result.\"\"\"\n \n", "problem_statement": "[Bug]: offloaded streaming tools retain an unconsumed output queue until completion\n### Prerequisites\r\n- [x] I searched existing issues and PRs.\r\n- [x] This is a reproducible bug.\r\n\r\n### Environment\r\nAgentScope main `27c52cc65088227bb7414cb665c1bbbdef18f220`, Python 3.12, Windows. No Docker or live model credentials are required.\r\n\r\n### Background / Description\r\nAfter ToolOffloadMiddleware returns its synthetic background response, `_drain_to_queue` continues adding every intermediate event to its unbounded queue. No consumer reads that queue anymore: the completion watcher awaits the drain task's final ToolResponse directly. Long-running streaming tools therefore retain all intermediate output until completion.\r\n\r\n### Observed result\r\nWith the real middleware, BackgroundTaskManager and InMemoryMessageBus, a gated stream emits 32 independent 256-KiB ToolChunks after offload. After garbage collection all 32 chunks are still live, the queue holds 32 entries, and at least 8 MiB of otherwise unneeded text is retained. The consuming control retains zero chunks. This is a deterministic synthetic workload, not a production memory benchmark.\r\n\r\n### Proposed fix\r\nDetach and release the foreground queue when ownership transfers to background execution, and stop enqueuing intermediate events after that boundary. Preserve the final ToolResponse and exactly-once completion delivery, including errors. Merely bounding the queue would block the producer forever because there is no consumer.\r\n\r\nRelated #3458/#3459 address delivery-task lifetime/errors, not retention while the tool is running. #3045 concerns foreground interruption and is outside this change.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nSave the following files together and run the `probe_*.py` file with AgentScope installed from the above revision. All resources are local and cleaned up.\r\n\r\n#### probe_offload_queue_retention.py\r\n```python\r\n\"\"\"Measure live streamed chunks after the offload consumer has returned.\"\"\"\r\nimport asyncio\r\nimport gc\r\nimport json\r\nimport weakref\r\nfrom types import SimpleNamespace\r\n\r\nfrom agentscope.app._manager import BackgroundTaskManager\r\nfrom agentscope.app.message_bus import InMemoryMessageBus\r\nfrom agentscope.app.middleware import ToolOffloadMiddleware\r\nfrom agentscope.message import TextBlock, ToolCallBlock\r\nfrom agentscope.tool import ToolChunk, ToolResponse\r\n\r\n\r\nasync def run(background):\r\n    bus = InMemoryMessageBus()\r\n    manager = BackgroundTaskManager(bus)\r\n    start, streamed, finish = asyncio.Event(), asyncio.Event(), asyncio.Event()\r\n    refs = []\r\n\r\n    async def lookup(_name):\r\n        return SimpleNamespace(is_state_injected=False, is_external_tool=False)\r\n\r\n    agent = SimpleNamespace(name=\"audit\", toolkit=SimpleNamespace(get_tool=lookup), state=SimpleNamespace(session_id=\"s1\"))\r\n    call = ToolCallBlock(id=\"call1\", name=\"stream\", input=\"{}\")\r\n\r\n    async def handler(**_kwargs):\r\n        await start.wait()\r\n        for i in range(32):\r\n            item = ToolChunk(content=[TextBlock(text=str(i) + \"x\" * (256 * 1024))])\r\n            refs.append(weakref.ref(item))\r\n            yield item\r\n            del item\r\n        streamed.set()\r\n        await finish.wait()\r\n        yield ToolResponse(id=\"call1\", content=[TextBlock(text=\"complete\")])\r\n\r\n    async def consume(iterator):\r\n        async for _ in iterator:\r\n            del _\r\n\r\n    async with bus, manager:\r\n        middleware = ToolOffloadMiddleware(manager, bus, \"u1\", \"a1\", timeout_secs=0.01)\r\n        iterator = middleware.on_acting(agent, {\"tool_call\": call}, handler) if background else handler()\r\n        consumer = asyncio.create_task(consume(iterator))\r\n        drain = None\r\n        try:\r\n            if background:\r\n                await asyncio.wait_for(consumer, 5)  # Synthetic response already returned.\r\n                assert len(manager.tasks) == 1\r\n                drain = next(iter(manager.tasks.values())).asyncio_task\r\n            start.set()\r\n            await asyncio.wait_for(streamed.wait(), 5)\r\n            gc.collect()\r\n            retained = sum(ref() is not None for ref in refs)\r\n            queued = drain.get_coro().cr_frame.f_locals[\"queue\"].qsize() if drain else 0\r\n            result = {\"background\": background, \"emitted_chunks\": 32, \"live_chunks_after_consumer_return\": retained, \"unconsumed_queue\": queued, \"retained_payload_bytes_at_least\": retained * 256 * 1024}\r\n            assert retained == (32 if background else 0), result\r\n            print(json.dumps(result))\r\n        finally:\r\n            start.set()\r\n            finish.set()\r\n            await asyncio.wait_for(consumer, 5)\r\n            if drain:\r\n                await asyncio.wait_for(drain, 5)\r\n            await asyncio.sleep(0)\r\n\r\n\r\nasync def main():\r\n    await run(False)\r\n    await run(True)\r\n\r\nasyncio.run(main())\r\n\r\n```\r\n\ntest(app): fix race in background task renewal fairness test\n## AgentScope Version\n\n2.0.12dev\n\n## Description\n\nFix an intermittent failure in\n`TestRedisBackgroundTaskRecords.test_renewal_budget_preserves_fairness_and_cancels_io`, introduced in #1865 and reported on Windows: `AssertionError: 0 not greater than or equal to 2`\n\nThe renewal scheduler starts during task registration, before the stalled-I/O mock is installed. When registration overlaps a renewal round, the test can observe all task IDs before either mocked head task has been cancelled.\n\nGate renewal with an `asyncio.Event` until all six tasks are registered and the mock is installed. This makes the initial queue order deterministic while preserving the fairness, concurrency, cancellation, and shutdown assertions.\n\nThis change only affects test setup and requires no migration or\nuser-facing docume\n\n## Checklist\n\nPlease check the following items before code is ready to be reviewed.\n\n- [ ]  An issue has been created for this PR\n- [ ]  I have read the [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ]  Docstrings are in Google style\n- [ ]  Related documentation has been updated (e.g. links, examples, etc.) in [documentation repository](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/docs)\n- [ ]  Code is ready for review\n", "hints_text": "/assign me\n", "created_at": "2026-11-09T09:14:21Z"}
{"repo": "agentscope-ai/agentscope", "pull_number": 3883, "instance_id": "agentscope-ai__agentscope-3883", "issue_numbers": ["1800"], "base_commit": "906d4ef743fbc28a4a967a4ae55adda008c7f6ff", "patch": "diff --git a/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/api/backgroundTask.ts b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/api/backgroundTask.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..bcfb7fe083\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/api/backgroundTask.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+import { client } from './client';\n+import type { ListBackgroundTasksResponse } from './types';\n+\n+export const backgroundTaskApi = {\n+\tlist: (sessionId: string, baseUrl: string, userId: string, signal: AbortSignal) =>\n+\t\tclient.get<ListBackgroundTasksResponse>(\n+\t\t\t'/background-tasks',\n+\t\t\t{ session_id: sessionId },\n+\t\t\t{ baseUrl, userId, signal, silent: true, timeoutMs: 10_000 },\n+\t\t),\n+};\ndiff --git a/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/api/client.ts b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/api/client.ts\nindex 47252d0ee9..8facbf302c 100644\n--- a/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/api/client.ts\n+++ b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/api/client.ts\n@@ -126,7 +126,13 @@ export const client = {\n \tget: <T>(\n \t\tpath: string,\n \t\tparams?: Record<string, string>,\n-\t\toptions?: { silent?: boolean; baseUrl?: string; userId?: string; timeoutMs?: number },\n+\t\toptions?: {\n+\t\t\tsilent?: boolean;\n+\t\t\tsignal?: AbortSignal;\n+\t\t\tbaseUrl?: string;\n+\t\t\tuserId?: string;\n+\t\t\ttimeoutMs?: number;\n+\t\t},\n \t) => request<T>(path, { method: 'GET', params, ...options }),\n \tpost: <T>(\n \t\tpath: string,\ndiff --git a/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/api/index.ts b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/api/index.ts\nindex 478592bdeb..b080bf5559 100644\n--- a/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/api/index.ts\n+++ b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/api/index.ts\n@@ -23,3 +23,4 @@ export type {\n export type { TTSModelCard } from './types';\n export { channelApi } from './channel';\n export { healthApi } from './health';\n+export { backgroundTaskApi } from './backgroundTask';\ndiff --git a/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/api/types.ts b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/api/types.ts\nindex c3e876b5fa..4774350e85 100644\n--- a/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/api/types.ts\n+++ b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/api/types.ts\n@@ -413,6 +413,31 @@ export interface SessionView {\n \tteam: TeamDetailResponse | null;\n }\n \n+// \u2500\u2500\u2500 Background tools \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n+\n+export type BackgroundTaskStatus = 'running' | 'completed' | 'failed' | 'cancelled';\n+\n+export interface BackgroundTaskInfo {\n+\ttask_id: string;\n+\tsession_id: string;\n+\tagent_id: string;\n+\ttool_name: string;\n+\tsummary: string;\n+\tstatus: BackgroundTaskStatus;\n+\t/** UTC date-time when the tool was registered for background execution. */\n+\tstarted_at: string;\n+\t/** Actual execution start, absent or null in records created by older servers. */\n+\texecution_started_at?: string | null;\n+\tcompleted_at: string | null;\n+\terror_summary: string | null;\n+}\n+\n+export interface ListBackgroundTasksResponse {\n+\ttasks: BackgroundTaskInfo[];\n+\t/** Includes retained terminal tasks; this is not the running count. */\n+\ttotal: number;\n+}\n+\n // \u2500\u2500\u2500 JSON Schema \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n \n /**\ndiff --git a/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/components/panel/BackgroundTasksPanel.tsx b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/components/panel/BackgroundTasksPanel.tsx\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..e3daabd082\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/components/panel/BackgroundTasksPanel.tsx\n@@ -0,0 +1,260 @@\n+import { formatDistanceStrict } from 'date-fns';\n+import { enUS, zhCN } from 'date-fns/locale';\n+import {\n+\tActivity,\n+\tCheck,\n+\tChevronDown,\n+\tCircleAlert,\n+\tCircleCheck,\n+\tCircleSlash,\n+\tCopy,\n+\tLoader2,\n+\tMessageSquare,\n+} from 'lucide-react';\n+import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';\n+\n+import type { BackgroundTaskInfo } from '@/api';\n+import { PanelEmpty } from '@/components/panel/PanelEmpty';\n+import { Badge } from '@/components/ui/badge';\n+import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';\n+import { Collapsible, CollapsibleContent, CollapsibleTrigger } from '@/components/ui/collapsible';\n+import { useTranslation } from '@/i18n/useI18n';\n+import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';\n+import { copyToClipboard } from '@/utils/common';\n+\n+const STATUS_ICONS = {\n+\trunning: Loader2,\n+\tcompleted: CircleCheck,\n+\tfailed: CircleAlert,\n+\tcancelled: CircleSlash,\n+};\n+\n+function BackgroundTaskRow({ task, now }: { task: BackgroundTaskInfo; now: number }) {\n+\tconst { t, i18n } = useTranslation();\n+\tconst [copied, setCopied] = useState(false);\n+\tconst Icon = STATUS_ICONS[task.status];\n+\tconst started = new Date(task.started_at).getTime();\n+\tconst ended = task.completed_at ? new Date(task.completed_at).getTime() : now;\n+\tconst duration = formatDistanceStrict(started, Math.max(started, ended), {\n+\t\tlocale: i18n.language.startsWith('zh') ? zhCN : enUS,\n+\t});\n+\tconst executionStarted = task.execution_started_at\n+\t\t? Date.parse(task.execution_started_at)\n+\t\t: null;\n+\tconst totalDuration =\n+\t\texecutionStarted !== null\n+\t\t\t? formatDistanceStrict(executionStarted, Math.max(executionStarted, ended), {\n+\t\t\t\t\tlocale: i18n.language.startsWith('zh') ? zhCN : enUS,\n+\t\t\t\t})\n+\t\t\t: null;\n+\n+\tuseEffect(() => {\n+\t\tif (!copied) return;\n+\t\tconst timer = window.setTimeout(() => setCopied(false), 2000);\n+\t\treturn () => window.clearTimeout(timer);\n+\t}, [copied]);\n+\n+\treturn (\n+\t\t<li className=\"min-w-0 rounded-xl border border-border/60 p-3\">\n+\t\t\t<div className=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-2\">\n+\t\t\t\t<span className=\"min-w-0 break-words text-sm font-medium [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\">\n+\t\t\t\t\t{task.tool_name}\n+\t\t\t\t</span>\n+\t\t\t\t<Badge\n+\t\t\t\t\tvariant=\"outline\"\n+\t\t\t\t\tclassName={cn('shrink-0 gap-1', task.status === 'failed' && 'text-destructive')}\n+\t\t\t\t>\n+\t\t\t\t\t<Icon\n+\t\t\t\t\t\tclassName={cn(\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t'size-3',\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttask.status === 'running' && 'motion-safe:animate-spin',\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t)}\n+\t\t\t\t\t/>\n+\t\t\t\t\t{t(`panel.background.status.${task.status}`)}\n+\t\t\t\t</Badge>\n+\t\t\t</div>\n+\t\t\t{task.summary && (\n+\t\t\t\t<p className=\"mt-2 whitespace-pre-wrap text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\">\n+\t\t\t\t\t{task.summary}\n+\t\t\t\t</p>\n+\t\t\t)}\n+\t\t\t<p className=\"mt-2 text-xs tabular-nums text-muted-foreground\">\n+\t\t\t\t{totalDuration !== null\n+\t\t\t\t\t? t('panel.background.totalDuration', { duration: totalDuration })\n+\t\t\t\t\t: t('panel.background.duration', { duration })}\n+\t\t\t</p>\n+\t\t\t{totalDuration !== null && (\n+\t\t\t\t<p className=\"mt-1 text-xs tabular-nums text-muted-foreground\">\n+\t\t\t\t\t{t('panel.background.backgroundDuration', { duration })}\n+\t\t\t\t</p>\n+\t\t\t)}\n+\t\t\t<div className=\"mt-1 flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1\">\n+\t\t\t\t<span className=\"shrink-0 text-xs text-muted-foreground\">ID</span>\n+\t\t\t\t<code\n+\t\t\t\t\tclassName=\"min-w-0 truncate text-xs text-muted-foreground\"\n+\t\t\t\t\ttitle={task.task_id}\n+\t\t\t\t>\n+\t\t\t\t\t{task.task_id}\n+\t\t\t\t</code>\n+\t\t\t\t<Button\n+\t\t\t\t\tvariant=\"ghost\"\n+\t\t\t\t\tsize=\"icon-xs\"\n+\t\t\t\t\taria-label={t(copied ? 'panel.background.copied' : 'panel.background.copyId')}\n+\t\t\t\t\ttooltip={t(copied ? 'panel.background.copied' : 'panel.background.copyId')}\n+\t\t\t\t\tonClick={async () => {\n+\t\t\t\t\t\tif (await copyToClipboard(task.task_id)) setCopied(true);\n+\t\t\t\t\t}}\n+\t\t\t\t>\n+\t\t\t\t\t{copied ? <Check /> : <Copy />}\n+\t\t\t\t</Button>\n+\t\t\t</div>\n+\t\t\t{task.status === 'failed' && task.error_summary && (\n+\t\t\t\t<Collapsible className=\"mt-2 border-t border-border/60 pt-2\">\n+\t\t\t\t\t<CollapsibleTrigger asChild>\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t<Button variant=\"ghost\" size=\"xs\" className=\"group px-0 text-destructive\">\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<ChevronDown className=\"transition-transform group-data-[state=open]:rotate-180\" />\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{t('panel.background.errorDetails')}\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t</Button>\n+\t\t\t\t\t</CollapsibleTrigger>\n+\t\t\t\t\t<CollapsibleContent>\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t<p className=\"mt-2 whitespace-pre-wrap text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\">\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{task.error_summary}\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n+\t\t\t\t\t</CollapsibleContent>\n+\t\t\t\t</Collapsible>\n+\t\t\t)}\n+\t\t</li>\n+\t);\n+}\n+\n+interface BackgroundTasksPanelProps {\n+\tsessionId: string | null;\n+\ttasks: BackgroundTaskInfo[] | undefined;\n+\tloading: boolean;\n+\terror: boolean;\n+\trefreshing: boolean;\n+\tvisible: boolean;\n+\tupdatedAt: number;\n+\tonRefresh: () => void;\n+}\n+\n+/** Read-only view of running tools and the server's retained terminal snapshots. */\n+export function BackgroundTasksPanel({\n+\tsessionId,\n+\ttasks,\n+\tloading,\n+\terror,\n+\trefreshing,\n+\tvisible,\n+\tupdatedAt,\n+\tonRefresh,\n+}: BackgroundTasksPanelProps) {\n+\tconst { t } = useTranslation();\n+\tconst [now, setNow] = useState(Date.now);\n+\tconst running = tasks?.filter((task) => task.status === 'running') ?? [];\n+\tconst recent =\n+\t\ttasks\n+\t\t\t?.filter((task) => task.status !== 'running')\n+\t\t\t.sort((a, b) => Date.parse(b.completed_at!) - Date.parse(a.completed_at!)) ?? [];\n+\tconst ticking = visible && !error && running.length > 0;\n+\n+\tuseEffect(() => {\n+\t\tif (!ticking) return;\n+\t\tsetNow(Date.now());\n+\t\tconst timer = window.setInterval(() => setNow(Date.now()), 1000);\n+\t\treturn () => window.clearInterval(timer);\n+\t}, [ticking]);\n+\n+\tif (!sessionId) {\n+\t\treturn <PanelEmpty icon={MessageSquare} title={t('panel.background.noSession')} />;\n+\t}\n+\tif (loading) {\n+\t\treturn (\n+\t\t\t<div\n+\t\t\t\trole=\"status\"\n+\t\t\t\tclassName=\"flex flex-1 items-center justify-center gap-2 p-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"\n+\t\t\t>\n+\t\t\t\t<Loader2 className=\"size-4 motion-safe:animate-spin\" />\n+\t\t\t\t{t('panel.loading')}\n+\t\t\t</div>\n+\t\t);\n+\t}\n+\n+\treturn (\n+\t\t<div className=\"flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-3 py-3\">\n+\t\t\t{error && (\n+\t\t\t\t<div\n+\t\t\t\t\trole=\"status\"\n+\t\t\t\t\tclassName=\"rounded-xl border border-destructive/20 bg-destructive/5 p-3\"\n+\t\t\t\t>\n+\t\t\t\t\t<p className=\"text-xs leading-relaxed\">\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t{t(tasks ? 'panel.background.stale' : 'panel.background.loadError')}\n+\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n+\t\t\t\t\t<Button\n+\t\t\t\t\t\tvariant=\"outline\"\n+\t\t\t\t\t\tsize=\"xs\"\n+\t\t\t\t\t\tclassName=\"mt-2\"\n+\t\t\t\t\t\tdisabled={refreshing}\n+\t\t\t\t\t\tonClick={onRefresh}\n+\t\t\t\t\t>\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t{t('common.retry')}\n+\t\t\t\t\t</Button>\n+\t\t\t\t</div>\n+\t\t\t)}\n+\t\t\t{tasks && tasks.length === 0 && !error && (\n+\t\t\t\t<PanelEmpty\n+\t\t\t\t\ticon={Activity}\n+\t\t\t\t\ttitle={t('panel.background.emptyTitle')}\n+\t\t\t\t\tdescription={t('panel.background.emptyDescription')}\n+\t\t\t\t/>\n+\t\t\t)}\n+\t\t\t{tasks && tasks.length > 0 && (\n+\t\t\t\t<>\n+\t\t\t\t\t{running.length > 0 ? (\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t<ul className=\"space-y-2\" aria-label={t('panel.background.status.running')}>\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{running.map((task) => (\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<BackgroundTaskRow\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tkey={task.task_id}\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttask={task}\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tnow={error ? updatedAt : now}\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t/>\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t))}\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n+\t\t\t\t\t) : (\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t<p className=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{t('panel.background.noRunning')}\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n+\t\t\t\t\t)}\n+\t\t\t\t\t{recent.length > 0 && (\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t<Collapsible className=\"min-w-0 border-t border-border/60 pt-2\">\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<CollapsibleTrigger asChild>\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<Button\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tvariant=\"ghost\"\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tsize=\"sm\"\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclassName=\"group w-full justify-between px-0\"\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{t('panel.background.recent', { count: recent.length })}\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<ChevronDown className=\"transition-transform group-data-[state=open]:rotate-180\" />\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</Button>\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</CollapsibleTrigger>\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<CollapsibleContent>\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p className=\"mb-3 mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground\">\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{t('panel.background.retention')}\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<ul className=\"space-y-2\">\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{recent.map((task) => (\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<BackgroundTaskRow\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tkey={task.task_id}\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttask={task}\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tnow={now}\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t/>\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t))}\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</CollapsibleContent>\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t</Collapsible>\n+\t\t\t\t\t)}\n+\t\t\t\t</>\n+\t\t\t)}\n+\t\t</div>\n+\t);\n+}\ndiff --git a/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/components/panel/PanelDock.tsx b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/components/panel/PanelDock.tsx\nindex 7cf5068024..aaa50e84f4 100644\n--- a/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/components/panel/PanelDock.tsx\n+++ b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/components/panel/PanelDock.tsx\n@@ -13,7 +13,14 @@ import { Separator } from '@/components/ui/separator';\n  * Identifier for a dockable panel. Used both as the React key and to\n  * look its descriptor up in {@link PanelDockProps.panels}.\n  */\n-export type PanelKey = 'plan' | 'mcp' | 'skill' | 'permission' | 'knowledge' | 'team';\n+export type PanelKey =\n+\t| 'plan'\n+\t| 'mcp'\n+\t| 'skill'\n+\t| 'permission'\n+\t| 'knowledge'\n+\t| 'team'\n+\t| 'background';\n \n /**\n  * The presentation of a single panel: header chrome plus its already\ndiff --git a/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/hooks/useBackgroundTasks.ts b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/hooks/useBackgroundTasks.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..7e77bba7c8\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/hooks/useBackgroundTasks.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@\n+import { useQuery, useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query';\n+import { useEffect, useMemo, useSyncExternalStore } from 'react';\n+\n+import { backgroundTaskApi } from '@/api';\n+import { getBaseUrl, getUserId } from '@/api/client';\n+\n+function subscribeVisibility(onChange: () => void) {\n+\tdocument.addEventListener('visibilitychange', onChange);\n+\treturn () => document.removeEventListener('visibilitychange', onChange);\n+}\n+\n+const isPageVisible = () => document.visibilityState === 'visible';\n+\n+/** Poll the selected session even when its last snapshot has no running tasks. */\n+export function useBackgroundTasks(sessionId: string | null, open: boolean) {\n+\tconst queryClient = useQueryClient();\n+\tconst visible = useSyncExternalStore(subscribeVisibility, isPageVisible);\n+\tconst baseUrl = getBaseUrl();\n+\tconst userId = getUserId();\n+\tconst queryKey = useMemo(\n+\t\t() => ['background-tasks', baseUrl, userId, sessionId],\n+\t\t[baseUrl, userId, sessionId],\n+\t);\n+\tconst active = open && visible && sessionId !== null;\n+\tconst query = useQuery({\n+\t\tqueryKey,\n+\t\tqueryFn: ({ signal }) => backgroundTaskApi.list(sessionId!, baseUrl, userId, signal),\n+\t\tenabled: active,\n+\t\tstaleTime: 0,\n+\t\tgcTime: 0,\n+\t\tretry: false,\n+\t\trefetchInterval: active ? 3000 : false,\n+\t\trefetchIntervalInBackground: false,\n+\t\trefetchOnWindowFocus: true,\n+\t});\n+\n+\t// Disabling a query stops its timer but does not abort an in-flight fetch.\n+\tuseEffect(() => {\n+\t\tif (!active) void queryClient.cancelQueries({ queryKey, exact: true });\n+\t}, [active, queryClient, queryKey]);\n+\n+\tuseEffect(\n+\t\t() => () => {\n+\t\t\tvoid queryClient.cancelQueries({ queryKey, exact: true });\n+\t\t},\n+\t\t[queryClient, queryKey],\n+\t);\n+\n+\treturn { ...query, visible };\n+}\ndiff --git a/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/i18n/locales/en.json b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/i18n/locales/en.json\nindex b147bf1cbb..0253ef626f 100644\n--- a/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/i18n/locales/en.json\n+++ b/examples/web_ui/frontend/src/i18n/locales/en.json\n@@ -663,6 +663,31 @@\n \t\t\"blockedBy\": \"blocked by\"\n \t},\n \t\"panel\": {\n+\t\t\"background\": {\n+\t\t\t\"title\": \"Background tools\",\n+\t\t\t\"runningCount\": \"Running: {{count}}\",\n+\t\t\t\"refresh\": \"Refresh background tools\",\n+\t\t\t\"duration\": \"Background duration: {{duration}}\",\n+\t\t\t\"totalDuration\": \"Total duration: {{duration}}\",\n+\t\t\t\"backgroundDuration\": \"Of which in background: {{duration}}\",\n+\t\t\t\"copyId\": \"Copy task ID\",\n+\t\t\t\"copied\": \"Task ID copied\",\n+\t\t\t\"errorDetails\": \"Failure details\",\n+\t\t\t\"noSession\": \"Select a conversation to view background tools\",\n+\t\t\t\"emptyTitle\": \"No background tools\",\n+\t\t\t\"emptyDescription\": \"Tools that continue running in the background will appear here.\",\n+\t\t\t\"noRunning\": \"No tools are running in the background.\",\n+\t\t\t\"recent\": \"Recently finished ({{count}})\",\n+\t\t\t\"retention\": \"Recent results are kept temporarily. This is not a complete history.\",\n+\t\t\t\"loadError\": \"Could not load background tools. Try again.\",\n+\t\t\t\"stale\": \"Could not refresh. Showing the last known status; tasks may have changed.\",\n+\t\t\t\"status\": {\n+\t\t\t\t\"runn